    ["game_files",
    ".SCHEMATIC",
    "Minecraft Schematic",
    "4.3",
    "A SCHEMATIC file is a schematic created by MCEdit, Tinkercad, or another Minecraft Java Edition modding tool. It contains an arrangement of blocks that comprise a structure (or structures) that can be placed in a Minecraft world. With the release of Minecraft Java Edition 1.13,.SCHEM files replaced SCHEMATIC files. Minecraft Java Edition is the original version of Minecraft. Notably, Minecraft Java Edition allows players to use a variety of unofficial add-ons and mods to enhance their gameplay. Some Minecraft mods allow players to save copies of their Minecraft structures, including homes, natural features, monuments, and even entire worlds, as SCHEMATIC files. Players can use SCHEMATIC files to open and edit their structures in third-party Minecraft modding programs like MCEdit, import their structures to another Minecraft world, and share their structures with other players over the Internet. SCHEMATIC files are saved in Minecrafts.NBT (Named Binary Tag) file format and contain a variety of binary data that specifies a structures size and composition. Each SCHEMATIC file defines a structures width, height, and length, as well as the materials and types of blocks of which the structure is composed. When Mojang released Minecraft Java Edition 1.13, modders discovered that, due to technical changes, they could no longer export and import structures as SCHEMATIC files. As a result, many mod developers chose to migrate from the SCHEMATIC format to the SCHEM format, which was created by the team behind Sponge, an open-source Minecraft modding framework. You can open and edit SCHEMATIC files using a variety of Minecraft mod tools. Most notably, you can open SCHEMATIC files in MCEdit (Windows, Linux), which is a Minecraft saved game editor. To open a SCHEMATIC file in MCEdit, select the Import button while editing a level. You can also export a structure as a SCHEMATIC file by selecting Export Schematic after selecting the structure. How can I convert a SCHEMATIC file to a SCHEM file? At the moment, there is no easy way to convert a Minecraft SCHEMATIC file to a SCHEM file. You can, however, convert SCHEM files to SCHEMATIC files, so the structures they contain can be used in pre-1.13 versions of Minecraft, using SchemToSchematic (Web) or Mineways (Windows). Windows MCEdit. WorldEdit. Redstone Simulator. Minecraft Note Block Studio —  (Discontinued). NBTExplorer. Mac WorldEdit. Redstone Simulator. NBTExplorer. Linux MCEdit. WorldEdit. Redstone Simulator. NBTExplorer. Web Javascript Redstone SimulatorFree.",
    "Windows MCEdit. WorldEdit. Redstone Simulator. Minecraft Note Block Studio —  (Discontinued). NBTExplorer. Mac WorldEdit. Redstone Simulator. NBTExplorer. Linux MCEdit. WorldEdit. Redstone Simulator. NBTExplorer. Web Javascript Redstone Simulator.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".PACKAGE",
    "Electronic Arts Game Package File",
    "4.3",
    "A PACKAGE file is a resource package file used by various Electronic Arts (EA) games, including The Sims 2, The Sims 3, The Sims 4, The Sims Online, Spore, SimCity 4, and SimCity (2013). It stores an archive of one or more game files, often in XML format, and may include 3D models, textures, sounds, and other game data, such as characters and neighborhood information. PACKAGE files are saved in EAs standard DBPF archive format. Many PACKAGE files can be edited and repackaged with SimPE, a free editor for The Sims 2. They may also be created and modified with The Sims 2 ContentManager, a program officially released by Electronic Arts for modifying The Sims 2 content. Windows Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. S3PE. Ambertation SimPE. SporeEdit. SporeMaster. SimCityPak. Mac Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts SimCity. Electronic Arts Spore. Archive containing contents of a Linux program and associated files; created with the Autopackage package management system for Linux; installed using the Autopackage installer program. Autopackage is intended for creating application installers rather than system level installers. Linux Autopackage. A PACKAGE file contains an art kit for FOREVER Artisan, a digital scrapbooking application. It stores scrapbooking content, such as page templates, cards, seasonal decorations, and creative splatters, which can be added to scrapbook projects. PACKAGE files are typically purchased and downloaded from the FOREVER online store and imported into the program. Digital art kits may also be saved in an SBKIT or PAKIT file. You can import a kit in Artisan by selecting Import content from the Home menu. NOTE: FOREVER was formerly known as Panstoria and Artisan is based off Storybook Creator, which was formerly known as Panstoria. Windows FOREVER Artisan. A PACKAGE file is an offline update package used by MOBILedit Forensic Express, a program used to extract and analyze mobile device data. It contains data used to update or add a feature to MOBILedit Forensic Express. Users download MOBILedit PACKAGE files from the Downloads section of the programs website. MOBILedit Forensic Express is an application that investigators can use to extract data from mobile devices and mobile device backups. They can then use MOBILedit Forensic Express to analyze the data and generate reports. Periodically, developer Compelson Labs releases updates and add-ons for MOBILedit Forensic Express. These updates are available in the programs online download center. After users log in to the download center, they can download all available updates. Each update is saved as a PACKAGE file. Users can then install their PACKAGE files in MOBILedit Forensic Express. To install a PACKAGE file in MOBILedit Forensic Express (Windows): Open MOBILedit Forensic Express. Select Check for updates. Select Import package. Navigate to and open your PACKAGE file. Windows MOBILedit Forensic Express.",
    "Windows Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. S3PE. Ambertation SimPE. SporeEdit. SporeMaster. SimCityPak. Mac Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts SimCity. Electronic Arts Spore. Linux Autopackage. Windows FOREVER Artisan. Windows MOBILedit Forensic Express.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".NDS",
    "Nintendo DS Game ROM",
    "4.3",
    "An NDS file contains a game ROM of a video game for the Nintendo DS (NDS) handheld gaming console. It contains the same data as the original NDS game cartridge and can be played in Windows, macOS, Linux, or Android with a Nintendo DS emulator. NDS files are typically used by gamers who enjoy playing retro, discontinued games on their computers. The gamers may create NDS files by dumping the game data from the original cartridge onto a computer and packaging it as an NDS file. Or gamers may download NDS files from game emulator websites that have already been dumped from game cartridges. There are a variety of emulators available for playing NDS games, including DeSmuME, NO$GBA, iDeaS Emulator, OpenEmu, and Exophase DraStic DS Emulator. Some features provided by emulators include enhanced game graphics, helpful gameplay settings, and new cheat options. NOTE: The NDS was released in 2004 and uses two screens, one of which that is touch-sensitive. DS stands for Dual Screen.. You can open an NDS file and play the Nintendo DS video game it contains in DeSmuMe (Windows, Mac), OpenEMU (Mac), RetroArch (cross-platform), Delta (iOS), DraStic (Android), and other Nintendo DS emulators. Mac DeSmuME. OpenEmu. RetroArch. Windows NO$GBA. DeSmuME. iDeaS Emulator. DSemu. Dualis. RetroArch. Linux DeSmuME. iDeaS Emulator. RetroArch. iOS Delta Emulator. RetroArch. Android Exophase DraStic DS Emulator. nds4droid. CPU Studio NDS Emulator. RetroArchFree. Disc project created by Nero, a program suite used for burning multimedia and other data to discs; allows the user to burn data while spanning the data across multiple discs (i.e., DiscSpan); supports CDs, DVDs, and Blu-ray discs. Windows Nero 2022.",
    "Mac DeSmuME. OpenEmu. RetroArch. Windows NO$GBA. DeSmuME. iDeaS Emulator. DSemu. Dualis. RetroArch. Linux DeSmuME. iDeaS Emulator. RetroArch. iOS Delta Emulator. RetroArch. Android Exophase DraStic DS Emulator. nds4droid. CPU Studio NDS Emulator. RetroArch. Windows Nero 2022.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".YDR",
    "Yu-Gi-Oh! Power of Chaos Replay File",
    "4.3",
    "Recording of a duel from Yu-Gi-Oh! Power of Chaos that can be played back at a later time; may be saved by one of the three Power of Chaos games: Yugi the Destiny, Kaiba the Revenge, and Joey the Passion. Yu-Gi-Oh! is a card-trading game for Windows developed by Konami. Windows Konami Yu-Gi-Oh! Power of Chaos. A YDR file contains a drawing created by YouiDraw Drawing, an online vector drawing program. It is saved in a proprietary format that stores information about the drawing, such as layer properties, text, shapes, patterns, images, and pen, pencil, and brush strokes. YDR file open in YouiDraw Drawing You can create a YDR file in YouiDraw Drawing by selecting File → Download to Local Disk. The drawing is then saved in the YDR file and downloaded by the web browser. You can open YDR files in YouiDraw Drawing by selecting File → Open from Local Disk. You can save YDR files by selecting File → Save or Save As. NOTE: YouiDraw provides three design-related web apps, which include Drawing, Logo Creator, and Painter. Web YouiDraw DrawingFree. A YDR file is a 3D model used in Grand Theft Auto V, an open-world action-adventure game published by Rockstar Games. It contains an object, such as a building, prop, or weapon, that appears in the game. YDR files are compressed with Zlib compression, and they can be decompressed to access the de-textured 3D model (.odr file) and textures stored within them. The Grand Theft Auto franchise has always inspired tech-savvy players to put their own, unique stamp on their favorite games. With the release of Grand Theft Auto V, GTA modders immediately set about figuring out how to modify and create their own YDR files, so they could add new buildings and props to the game. Most players extract YDR files from Grand Theft Auto V using OpenIV, a popular Grand Theft Auto mod utility. After extracting a YDR file from Grand Theft Auto V, GTA V modders can open the file in AutoDesk 3DS Max using the player-created GIMS Evo plug-in. They can then modify the file as they see fit before exporting it and loading it into GTA V using OpenIV. For more complete instructions, refer to this YouTube video. Windows AutoDesk 3DS Max with GIMS Evo plug-in installed. OpenIV. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto V.",
    "Windows Konami Yu-Gi-Oh! Power of Chaos. Web YouiDraw Drawing. Windows AutoDesk 3DS Max with GIMS Evo plug-in installed. OpenIV. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto V.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".MPM",
    "Max Payne Mod",
    "4.3",
    "An MPM file is a mod for Rockstar Games Max Payne. It contains data used to import a custom level into the game or modify an existing level. For example, an MPM file might contain custom game logic that modifies how Max Paynes weapons behave. Max Payne is a popular third-person shooter video game in which players play as a New York City police detective named Max Payne. Rockstar Games released Max Payne in 2001. Those playing the Windows version of Max Payne can use MPM files to modify the games content. To do so, a player must place the MPM file in Max Paynes installation directory. Modders can also use Max Payne modding tools, such as RASMaster and MaxPaynePacker, to unpack MPM files and customize their contents. You can use RASMaster (Windows) or MaxPaynePacker (Windows) to extract an MPM files contents. You can also use these tools to package files into an MPM file. To use an MPM file as a Max Payne mod, place the file in Max Payne 2s installation directory, alongside its.exe file. Then, you can select your mod from the games Choose Customized Game menu option. Windows Rockstar Games Max Payne. RASMaster. MaxPaynePackerFree.",
    "Windows Rockstar Games Max Payne. RASMaster. MaxPaynePacker.",
    "?"],
