    "Cube 2: Sauerbraten Demo File ",
    "4.0",
    "Game file created by Cube 2: Sauerbraten, a free first-person shooter game; contains a recording of a single or multiplayer session; includes the player movements, game events, and chat log; enables Cube 2: Sauerbraten to replicate an exact replay of the game. Cube 2: Sauerbraten game clients can download DMO files from the host server that recorded the demo. Once downloaded, they can be played in local mode. NOTE: DMO files do not contain video data. If you would like to record a video session, use Cube 2: Sauerbratens movie recording functionality to save an.AVI file. Windows Cube 2: Sauerbraten. Mac Cube 2: Sauerbraten. Linux Cube 2: SauerbratenFree. File created by Duke Nukem 3D, a first-person shooter game developed with the Build game engine; contains a game recording of player actions and world events; enables players to replay multiplayer sessions. Windows Apogee Duke Nukem 3D. Demo of math functions recognized and run by Derive, the mathematical assistant for your PC. Windows Texas Instruments Derive. Movie database created with Movienizer, a movie organization program; includes information about each movie, such as actors, producers, and color posters; also keeps track of which movies are owned, loaned to others, or in a wish list. Windows Movienizer.",
    "Windows Cube 2: Sauerbraten. Mac Cube 2: Sauerbraten. Linux Cube 2: Sauerbraten. Windows Apogee Duke Nukem 3D. Windows Texas Instruments Derive. Windows Movienizer.",
