    ["game_files",
    ".IWD",
    "Call of Duty Game Data File",
    "3.9",
    "Contains game data used by Call of Duty 2 (CoD2) and Call of Duty 4; may store graphics, weapons, scripts, or other information; compressed using ZIP compression to save disk space. Most IWD files are stored in the /Program Files/Activision/Call of Duty/main/ directory. They can be unzipped using a file decompression program like WinZip and edited with a text editor. NOTE: Do not manually open IWD files unless you know exactly what changes to make. Altering an IWD file may make it unusable by Call of Duty. Windows Activision Call of Duty 2. Activision Call of Duty 4: Modern Warfare. Corel WinZip. Mac Activision Call of Duty 2 for Mac Activision Call of Duty 4: Modern Warfare.",
    "Windows Activision Call of Duty 2. Activision Call of Duty 4: Modern Warfare. Corel WinZip. Mac Activision Call of Duty 2 for Mac Activision Call of Duty 4: Modern Warfare.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".SPB",
    "Flight Simulator Mission File",
    "3.9",
    "Saved game file created by Microsoft ESP, a software toolkit used for flight and vehicle simulation; saves the state of a flight simulator mission, including the state of mission triggers and actions; saved with a.FLT file as part of a game save. Microsoft ESP missions are originally created in an XML format, but are saved in a binary SPB format. To convert a Flight Simulator X SPB file back into XML, use the spb2xml program. NOTE: Microsoft ESP technology is used in games such as Microsoft Flight Simulator X. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition. spb2xmlFree. Mobile phone backup file created by Samsung Kies, a synchronization tool for Samsung mobile phones; stores a backup of phonebook contacts; used for restoring contacts as well as for transferring contacts between phones. Windows Samsung KiesFree.",
    "Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition. spb2xml. Windows Samsung Kies.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".SMS",
    "Sega Master System ROM",
    "3.9",
    "ROM image of an original Sega Master System (SMS) video game; contains the same data stored on the actual game cartridge; can be played on a Mac or PC using SMS emulation software. The original Sega console was called the Sega Master System (SMS). It was released shortly after the original Nintendo Entertainment System (NES). NOTE: MESS and MacMESS can be used to load SMS games, but you need a valid ROM system image in order to load them. Windows Fusion. FreezeSMS. MESS. Meka. SMSPLUS. Mac SMS Plus. MacMESS. MasterGear. Linux MasterGearFree. A group of SMS text messages exported from a Sony Ericsson cell phone; saved in a text format that can be viewed with cell phone software or a basic text editor. Windows FJ Software MyPhoneExplorer. Any text editor Mac Any text editor.",
    "Windows Fusion. FreezeSMS. MESS. Meka. SMSPLUS. Mac SMS Plus. MacMESS. MasterGear. Linux MasterGear. Windows FJ Software MyPhoneExplorer. Any text editor. Mac Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".STR",
    "PlayStation Video Stream",
    "3.9",
    "Text file that defines the structure of a dBASE database; contains a list of all objects that can be included in the database file; includes the number, names, and widths of each field in the database. STR files can be used by dBASE to create printed archive index tables or to document the structure of each table. Windows dBase. An STR file is a video included in a PlayStation (PS1) video game. It contains a cinematic played in the game. Many games include STR files. Most gamers will never encounter STR files. However, some dedicated gamers have created utilities that allow them to extract STR files from PS1 games. This allows them to play STR files and convert them to more common video formats, using PlayStation game data utilities. Some games that use STR files include: MediEvil PGA Tour 97 Urban Chaos Chicken Run Harry Potter and the Sorcerers Stone Final Fantasy IX NOTE: STR files use audio saved in the.XA format. You can open an STR file and play the video it contains with jPSXdec (multiplatform), PSMPlay (Windows), or PsxMC (Windows). You can use jPSXdec, PSMPlay, or PsxMC to convert STR videos to the.AVI video format. Windows File Viewer Plus. PsxMC. PSMPlay. PSXPlay. jPSXdec. Mac jPSXdec. Linux jPSXdecFree. Object string file used by X-Plane, a professional flight simulator; contains data that defines the placement of objects in the simulator. The STR file uses the standard X-Plane format, which consists of a header and commands that define different aspects of the objects and their placement on the line. The STR format uses object strings, which are objects placed along a bezier curve. The file is designed to place objects in the X-Plane simulator but is primarily used to build airport taxiway lights. Windows X-Plane. Mac X-Plane. Linux X-Plane. Strings file used by WPS Office (previously known as Kingsoft Office), an office suite which includes the Writer, Spreadsheets, and Presentation applications; contains information used to configure the apps interface, which includes the placement and appearance of shapes, panes, and borders; also defines the appearance of text that appears in the window titles, buttons, menu texts, and other interface elements. NOTE: The STR file is located in the following directory: /​Kingsoft/​WPS Office/​office[version]/​mui/​default/​tips. Windows Kingsoft WPS Office. Screensaver used by Windows computers; contains animations, pictures, text, or moving patterns that fill the screen when the computer has been idle for a specific amount of time; can be selected within the Displays control panel. Most screensavers have a.SCR extension. Windows Used by the Windows operating system. An STR file is a livestream recording created by YouTube. It contains the content of a users live streaming event. YouTube saves livestreams in files named livestream.str. YouTube allows users to broadcast live streaming video to their channels, so they can interact with their audience in real-time. After a user finishes a livestream, they can upload it to their channel as they would a normal video. To allows users to upload livestreams, YouTube saves those livestreams in its backend as STR files. Users using the YouTube livestream API can retrieve their channels STR files from YouTubes servers. Other YouTube users are unlikely to encounter STR files, except when publishing a previous livestream as a channel video. Livestream.str - The default name YouTube assigns to livestream recordings. STR files are not meant to be opened by users. YouTube stores STR files and uses them to publish livestream recordings as channel videos. Web YouTubeFree. File used by Lord of the Rings (LOTR): Battle for Middle Earth II (BFME2), a real-time strategy game based off of the LOTR books and movies; saved in a plain text format and contains text strings that display tooltips, cutscene subtitles, and other textual data. Windows Electronic Arts Lord of the Rings: Battle for Middle Earth 2 —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows dBase. Windows File Viewer Plus. PsxMC. PSMPlay. PSXPlay. jPSXdec. Mac jPSXdec. Linux jPSXdec. Windows X-Plane. Mac X-Plane. Linux X-Plane. Windows Kingsoft WPS Office. Windows Used by the Windows operating system. Web YouTube. Windows Electronic Arts Lord of the Rings: Battle for Middle Earth 2 —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".CON",
    "Battlefield 1942 Configuration File",
    "3.9",
    "File used by Battlefield 1942, a World War II first-person shooter game; saved in plain text and contains configuration information for the game, including video and input control settings; often used for fine-tuning game mods.. Common CON files include video.con, videoDefault.con, maplist.con, and maplist.con. Windows Electronic Arts Battlefield 1942. Source file of an application written for the Concept Application Server; allows bi-directional communication between the user and the server. Can be accessed with a Web browser if the Concept Client (included with the Concept Server package) is installed. Concept URLs begin with concept:// such as: concept://my.server.com/my_application/main.con. Windows Run with RadGs Concept Application Server View in a Web browser with Concept Client installed Linux Run with RadGs Concept Application Server. A CON file is a settings file used by the COW operating system, which is an operating system based on Linux for select mobile devices. It contains setting parameters that configure various elements of the COW operating system, such as the path to the.MP3 ringtone that plays during an incoming phone call. CON files are saved in plain text format and can be opened using a text editor. You most likely will not encounter CON files because they are typically hidden on the device and are not meant to be opened. Windows Any text editor Mac Any text editor Linux Any text editor.",
    "Windows Electronic Arts Battlefield 1942. Windows Run with RadGs Concept Application Server View in a Web browser with Concept Client installed. Linux Run with RadGs Concept Application Server. Windows Any text editor. Mac Any text editor. Linux Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".CHESSTITANSSAVE-MS",
    "Microsoft Chess Titans Saved Game",
    "3.9",
    "Saved game file created by Chess Titans, a chess game included with Microsoft Games for Windows; saves the state of the chess board when the user exited the program and chose the Save button to save the current progress; allows users to continue where they last left off the next time the program is opened. CHESSTITANSSAVE-MS files are saved automatically by the game to the [user]/​Saved Games/​Microsoft Games/​Chess Titans/​ directory. NOTE: Chess Titans is only available with Windows 7. Windows Microsoft Chess Titans.",
    "Windows Microsoft Chess Titans.",
    "?"],
