    ["game_files",
    ".IVT",
    "International Volleyball 2006 Data File",
    "3.6",
    "Game data file referenced by International Volleyball 2006, a 3D volleyball game; may include data such as player information, game rules, actions, or graphics used by the game. Windows AddGames Italia International Volleyball 2006. Data table created by Beyond 20/20 statistical analysis and data visualization software; can be shared via the Web using Beyond 20/20 software; uses an OLAP system that is compatible with Microsoft Web technologies. IVT files can be viewed on a desktop computer using the Professional Browser desktop application, or they can be viewed through a Web browser using the Perspective and Web Data Server (WDS) Web applications. Windows Beyond 20/20 Professional Browser.",
    "Windows AddGames Italia International Volleyball 2006. Windows Beyond 20/20 Professional Browser.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".ACX",
    "Atari ST Program",
    "3.6",
    "An ACX file is a program written for Atari ST, a line of Atari computers from the 1980s. It may be a game or other type of application, such as a word processor or graphics editor. It is an executable file that a user can run on a computer with Atari ST emulation software. Atari introduced the Atari ST line in 1985 and released several ST models, including 520ST and 1040ST. However, Atari discontinued the Atari ST line in 1993. Retro computing enthusiasts utilize emulation software to run applications and play games on their modern computers. For example, a nostalgic computer user who enjoyed the Atari 1040ST computer from 1986 may install the Gemulator on their application to run a game saved as an ACX file. You can open an ACX file with various Atari ST emulators and run the program it contains. Atari ST emulators that support ACX files include Gemulator (Windows), Hatari (multiplatform), and PaCifiST (Windows). Windows Gemulator. PaCifiST. Hatari. Echo. FAST. SainT. STew. Mac Hatari. Linux HatariFree.",
    "Windows Gemulator. PaCifiST. Hatari. Echo. FAST. SainT. STew. Mac Hatari. Linux Hatari.",
    "?"],
