    ["game_files",
    ".SYSTEM",
    "Vega Strike Virtual System File",
    "2.6",
    "File used by Vega Strike, a space simulator game where players trade, fight, and explore in outer space; contains a space system, which includes the name, background graphics, number of stars, light properties, and planets. SYSTEM files can be used to created custom systems. They are stored in an XML format and can be edited with a text editor. Windows Vega Strike Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. gVim. Other text editor Mac Vega Strike Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Linux Vega Strike Other text editor.",
    "Windows Vega Strike Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. gVim. Other text editor. Mac Vega Strike Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Linux Vega Strike Other text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".PGF",
    "Pokémon Mystery Gift for Black & White File",
    "2.6",
    "A PGF file is a bitmap image created in the Progressive Graphics File (PGF) format. It supports lossy and lossless compression and a variety of color models, including indexed color (256 palette size), grayscale, RGB color, ARGB color, l*a*b color, and CMYK color. The PGF format was designed to improve on the JPEG standard by reducing compression time and increasing compression ratios. The format offers progressive transmission, which means the image can be viewed at a low quality before all of its data is fully downloaded and then increases as more data is received. The format also includes representation of multiple resolutions, which means that it does not need to store separate preview images, such as thumbnails. NOTE:PGF was developed at the same time as JPEG 2000 and initially released in 2000. The format was developed at the Institute of Theoretical Computer Science at ETH Zurich university. Windows NCH Software PhotoPad Photo Editor. libPGF. Mac Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. libPGF. Linux libPGFFree. Game file used by Pokémon Black and Pokémon White, the fifth generation of Pokémon games for the Nintendo DS game device; stores data for a mystery gift, which can be given to other players to unlock items and events in the game. PGF files are located within Pokémon saved games (.SAV files) on Nintendo DS cartridges. They can be edited and imported into a SAV file using Pokesav or the Pokémon Mystery Gift Editor. Windows Pokémon Mystery Gift EditorFree.",
    "Windows NCH Software PhotoPad Photo Editor. libPGF. Mac Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. libPGF. Linux libPGF. Windows Pokémon Mystery Gift Editor.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".MDL",
    "Luigis Mansion 3D Model File",
    "2.6",
    "An MDL file is a simulation model created using Simulink, a simulation and model-based design application. It contains the block diagram and block properties of a simulation. MDL files are saved in a plain text format and typically include a list of objects. Each object contains a set of properties and values that are delimited by line breaks. NOTE: The MDL format was replaced by the.SLX model format with the release of Simulink 2012. You can open an MDL file in MathWorks Simulink. If you do not have MathWorks Simulink, you can open an MDL file using any text editor, including: Notepad++ (Windows) TextEdit (Mac) Atom If you cannot open an MDL file in MathWorks Simulink, you can try changing the files extension to SLX. This will usually allow you to open the file in Simulink. Windows MathWorks Simulink. Mac MathWorks Simulink. Linux MathWorks Simulink. An MDL file is a model file used by Warcraft III, a real-time strategy game developed by Blizzard Entertainment. It stores a 3D model, including objects, meshes, and textures for buildings and units. MDL files allow text-based editing of model properties before generating a binary.MDX file used by Warcraft III. MDL files use a nested structure to create model properties. For example, a material element may include a layer property which in turn defines a transparent property for the layer. NOTE: MDL files are the text version of MDX 3D model binary files. They can be converted to the MDX format using the MDLX Converter program. From there, you can use several modeling tools to edit the model. Windows MDLX Converter. Blizzard Warcraft 3 Art Tools. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Notepad++. Other text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor. An MDL file is a three-dimensional model used for characters and creatures in the Half-Life video game. It is created using polygons and texture mapping for detail. MDL models can be seen from different views (wireframe, flatshaded, smoothshaded, and textured) using the Half-Life Model Viewer. NOTE: QC files are actually used by Valves Source game engine, so they are not restricted to Half-Life models. Windows chUmbaLum sOft Half-Life Model Viewer. chUmbaLum sOft MilkShape 3D. MDLDecompiler. Valve Half-Life. Valve Half-Life 2. Valve Source. Mac Valve Half-Life 2. Linux chUmbaLum sOft Half-Life Model ViewerFree. An MDL file is a three-dimensional model of an airplane or other aircraft used by Microsoft Flight Simulator. MDL is a standard model format used by multiple versions of the Flight Simulator series. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition. An MDL file is a diagram or model created by Rational Rose software. It is used for modeling software architecture and design, and creating business models that improve predictability and productivity. Windows IBM Rational Rose —  (Discontinued). Linux IBM Rational Rose —  (Discontinued). An MDL file is an audio tracking module file saved in the DigiTrakker Module (MDL) format, a proprietary format used by the Prodatron DigiTrakker audio application. It contains sequences, note patterns, and sound samples that represent different instruments played back based on the notes. MDL files also store metadata about the module, including the version. MDL file open in OpenMPT 1 Prodatron developed DigiTrakker and released it in 1995 for MS-DOS. Its MDL format is one of many module formats audio tracker developers released in the 1990s based on the.MOD Amiga Module format introduced in 1987. The last version of Digitrakker was 3.2. Prodatron discontinued the software in January 1997, but you may still encounter MDL files created by music enthusiasts using the original application or a third-party application that supports the MDL format. You can open an MDL file with OpenMPT in Windows by selecting File → Open.. MODPlug Player (Windows) and CocoModX (macOS) also support MDL files but are discontinued. Windows OpenMPT. MODPlug Player —  (Discontinued). Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). An MDL file is a CAD file created by Lectra Modaris, a clothing design application. It saves the cutters must list (or direction card) as well as the geometry for the pieces of the garment. MDL files are used for saving new fashion designs in mens, womens, and childrens clothing. When a design is complete, it can be sent to a machine cutter that cuts the designed patterns in a roll of fabric or another material. Windows Lectra Modaris. PAD Pattern Design. An MDL file is a model file used by Luigis Mansion, a Nintendo GameCube game. It stores 3D model data for characters, including Luigi, and objects that appear in the game. Luigis Mansion mainly uses the MDL format for its models but also uses the.BMD model format for some models in the game. NOTE: The mdl2obj tool can open Luigis Mansion MDL files and convert them into.OBJ files. Windows mdl2objFree.",
    "Windows MathWorks Simulink. Mac MathWorks Simulink. Linux MathWorks Simulink. Windows MDLX Converter. Blizzard Warcraft 3 Art Tools. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Notepad++. Other text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor. Windows chUmbaLum sOft Half-Life Model Viewer. chUmbaLum sOft MilkShape 3D. MDLDecompiler. Valve Half-Life. Valve Half-Life 2. Valve Source. Mac Valve Half-Life 2. Linux chUmbaLum sOft Half-Life Model Viewer. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition. Windows IBM Rational Rose —  (Discontinued). Linux IBM Rational Rose —  (Discontinued). Windows OpenMPT. MODPlug Player —  (Discontinued). Mac CocoModX —  (Discontinued). Windows Lectra Modaris. PAD Pattern Design. Windows mdl2obj.",
    "OpenMPT can convert MDL files to the following formats:.MID - MIDI File.IT - Impulse Tracker Module.WAV - WAVE Audio File.FLAC -. Lossless Audio Codec File.AU - Audacity Audio File.OPUS - Opus Audio File.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio File.RAW - Raw Audio Data.MP3 - MP3 Audio File."],
    ["game_files",
    ".NSBTX",
    "Nintendo DS Model Texture File",
    "2.6",
    "Texture file that can be applied to a Nintendo DS model (.NSBMD file); contains textures saved in a bitmap image format; can be mapped onto a 3D model to alter the appearance of the models surface. Windows MKDS Course ModifierFree.",
    "Windows MKDS Course Modifier.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".VIS",
    "Visibility Image File",
    "2.6",
    "Script created by Visual Importer, a data conversion application; saves in a plain text format and stores data conversion settings recorded from the softwares wizard walkthrough process; transforms data between source and destination formats when run in the software. VIS scripts save information such as the source data format (plain text, MS Access, MySQL,.CSV, etc.) as well as the destination format. They can also save database connection information and rules for converting data between database records, spreadsheet cells, and plain text. NOTE: VIS files are also referred to as VImp files. Windows DB Software Laboratory Visual Importer. Image information format developed for simulation purposes that includes scenery and maps; used by video games, such as Microsoft Flight Simulator 95 and 98 and other flight simulation programs. VIS files are saved in a text format that may be viewed in a text editor. However, they typically should not be opened or edited by the user. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition.",
    "Windows DB Software Laboratory Visual Importer. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".JIGSAW",
    "Jigsaw Explorer Save File",
    "2.6",
    "Save file created by Jigsaw Explorer, a browser-based jigsaw puzzle program; uses XML formatting and saves the current puzzle; enables puzzles to be saved to the desktop even though the program runs in the browser. NOTE: Jigsaw Explorer uses Microsoft Silverlight technology and requires the Silverlight Web browser plug-in to be installed before running the program in the Web browser. Web Carolina Road Jigsaw ExplorerFree.",
    "Web Carolina Road Jigsaw Explorer.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".GCS",
    "GameCube SharkSave File",
    "2.6",
    "Project file used by Cineform Studio, a video editor/converter software; once you create a project the GCS file is created. GoPro Cineform Studio enables the user to import footage from the 3D HERO System and convert it into viewable 3D files. The 3D HERO System is comprised of 2 HD HERO 1080p cameras that can record video and photos in 2D and 3D at the same time. Some editing features available with the GoPro Cineform Studio software include: saturation, contrast, exposure, frame-rate adjustment for slow motion, zoom, and cropping. After the user finishes their project they can then export their compressed side-by-side project into a.MOV file and watch it online at sites like YouTube or on their 2D or 3D TV. Windows GoPro Cineform Studio —  (Discontinued). Mac GoPro Cineform Studio —  (Discontinued). GameCube saved game also called a SharkSave file; created with the GameShark for the Nintendo GameCube, a cheat program for GameCube games; allows games to be saved whenever the user chooses to save the gameplay; may be opened with a supporting GameCube emulator. Windows Dolphin. Mac Dolphin. Linux DolphinFree.",
    "Windows GoPro Cineform Studio —  (Discontinued). Mac GoPro Cineform Studio —  (Discontinued). Windows Dolphin. Mac Dolphin. Linux Dolphin.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".MINESWEEPERSAVE-MS",
    "Minesweeper Saved Game",
    "2.6",
    "Saved game file created by Minesweeper, a classic puzzle game included with Microsoft Windows; stores the state of the minesweeper map, including revealed blocks, flagged blocks, and the elapsed time; used for restoring the last opened game state when the program was closed. You cannot save Minesweeper saved games from within Minesweeper program menu. Instead, when closing the program, it asks if the user would like to save the current state. If the user chooses to save the state, the game resumes the next time the program is opened. In Windows 7, MINESWEEPER-MS files are saved by default to the following directory: [user]/​Saved Games/​Microsoft Games/​Minesweeper/​. Windows Microsoft Minesweeper.",
    "Windows Microsoft Minesweeper.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BRSEQ",
    "Binary Revolution Sequence Format File",
    "2.6",
    "A BRSEQ file contains data in the Binary Revolution SEQuence (BRSEQ) format, which is used by various Nintendo Wii games. It stores audio data played by the game as a sound effect or background music that is looped during gameplay. BRSEQ files are typically packaged in.BRSAR audio archives included with the Wii game. BRSEQ files are not meant to be opened by Wii gamers. They are packaged with Wii games that are referenced by the game when played on a Wii console. However, some gamers enjoy modifying gameplay and extract BRSEQ files from BRSAR archives in order to alter them. You can convert BRSEQ files to the.MID file format using the rseq2midi tool in Windows. NOTE: BRSEQ files are typically only found in BRSAR archives packaged with the Mario Kart Wii game. Windows rseq2midiFree.",
    "Windows rseq2midi.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".CAH",
    "5e Companion App Character File",
    "2.6",
    "A CAH file contains information about a Dungeons & Dragons (D&D) character created with 5e Companion App, an Android app for managing characters used in D&D play. It stores information in plain text, which includes attributes and skills for the character. You will most likely only encounter CAH files if you enjoy playing D&D and use Companion App to manage your characters. The files are meant to only be opened with 5e Companion App. You can open a CAH file with 5e Companion App, which is only for Android devices. Since the CAH file is saved in plain text format, you can also open it with a text editor by changing the.cah file extension to.txt. However, the information will not be displayed the same way as if you opened the file with 5e Companion App. Android 5e Companion App.",
    "Android 5e Companion App.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".ECW",
    "EclipseCrossword Word List File",
    "2.6",
    "An ECW file is an image saved in the Enhanced Compression Wavelet (ECW) format. It was likely created using aerial photography or satellite imaging. Geographers and other Earth scientists use the images ECW files contain in GIS applications. ECW file open in QGIS Earth Resource Mapping, an Australian-based software company, developed the ECW format in 1998. The format has since become widely used in the geographical sciences community, because it efficiently compresses the large images created by aerial and satellite imaging. This allows geographers to more easily store geographical images and load them in GIS applications, which are used to analyze data about the Earths surface. In addition to image data, an ECW file can also contain map projection data, used to map the two-dimensional image the file contains to the Earths curvature. Each ECW file can contain up to 65,535 bands, which are layers or colors that can be viewed separately in the image. NOTE: Leica Geosystems now owns the rights to the ECW format. You can open an ECW file with ESRI ArcGIS for Desktop (Windows), QGIS (Windows, Mac), and several other GIS applications. For example, to open an ECW file with QGIS, drag the file to the open program window. Then, the image your ECW file contains will appear in QGIS. Windows ERDAS IMAGINE. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Safe Software FME Desktop. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. TatukGIS Viewer. QGIS. Mac Safe Software FME Desktop. QGIS. Linux Safe Software FME Desktop. An ECW file contains a crossword created by EclipseCrossword, a program used to generate crossword puzzles. It contains a crossword puzzle, which includes each word with its clue and whether it is down or across. ECW files also include the title, author, copyright, and letter width and height of the puzzle. You can open ECW files in EclipseCrossword. However, the program is only available for Windows. If you come across an ECW file in macOS you can open the ECW file with a text editor since the file is stored in plain text. You can print crosswords stored in ECW files and save them as webpages in EclipseCrossword. You can also publish ECW puzzles as.RTF,.WMF,.EPS files. Windows Green Eclipse EclipseCrosswordFree.",
    "Windows ERDAS IMAGINE. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Safe Software FME Desktop. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. TatukGIS Viewer. QGIS. Mac Safe Software FME Desktop. QGIS. Linux Safe Software FME Desktop. Windows Green Eclipse EclipseCrossword.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BF",
    "Ubisoft BigFile Game Data Archive",
    "2.6",
    "Game data archive format used by games developed by Cryo Interactive Entertainment; contains game data, such as objects, maps, sounds, and music in a single archive. Microïds acquired Cryo Interactive in 2008, but several Microïds games still use the CryoBF format. The following games use BF files to store game data: Nostradamus: The Last Prophecy Safecracker: The Ultimate Puzzle Adventure Destination: Treasure Island Return to Mysterious Island Return to Mysterious Island 2: Minas Fate The Secret of the Nautilus Dracula 3: The Path of the Dragon BF files are referenced by the games above and are not meant to be opened manually. However, the contents of a BF file can be extracted using an unpacking program like Unpakke. Windows XpoZeds UnpakkeFree. A BF file is a source code file written in the Brainf*ck programming language. It contains a program that is meant to be compiled using a Brainf*ck compiler. BF files contain only the characters <, >, +, -,., ,, [, and ], as well as development comments. In 1992, Urban Müller created the Brainf*ck programming language. When creating Brainf*ck, Müllers goal was to create a language that could be compiled using the smallest-possible compiler. As such, the language includes only eight commands, each of which is implemented using a single character. These characters include: < > + -. , [ ] While the Brainf*ck language is quite impractical, some other developers have latched onto the esoteric language and its structure. When these developers create Brainf*ck programs, they typically save them in BF files. An example Brainf*ck program, saved within a BF file, might look like this: ++++++++[>++++[>++>+++>+++>+<<<<-]>+>+>→>+[<]<-]>>.>---.+++++++.+++.>>.<-.<.+++.------.--------.>>+.>++. NOTE: Brainf*ck source code is also saved using the.B extension. Because BF files are plain text files, you can open and examine them using any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or Github Atom (cross-platform). If you want to run the Brainf*ck program a BF file contains, you can do so using a Brainf*ck development environment or interpreter, such as Brainf*ck Interpreter (Web, Android). Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor Windows bfbuilder. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor Linux Vim. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor Web Brainf*ck Interpreter. Android Brainf*ck Interpreter. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS. A BF file is a custom font project file created by BirdFont. It contains XML-formatted text that describes a custom font. BF files are used to export fonts in common font formats, such as.TTF,.OTF,.EOT, and.SVG. BF file open in Birdfont Birdfont is a font design program that allows users to create, import, and edit fonts. The program is available in both free and commercial versions, which contain many but not all of the same features. For example, the free version of Birdfont can export only fonts created under the SIL Open Font License. When a Birdfont user saves an in-progress font design project, the project is saved as a BF file. BF files are XML files, meaning they contain plain text that is organized using an XML schema and elements. This text describes the font the user has created in Birdfont. For example, the <collection> element denotes the beginning of a new font character description. However, when opened in Birdfont, BF files do not appear as XML files. Instead, they appear as font stylesheets that a user can interact with and edit graphically, instead of via text. You can open a BF file in Birdfont (cross-platform). To do so, select Birdfonts sandwich menu (located in the programs upper right-hand corner), select File → Open, and then navigate to and open your BF file. The font your file describes will appear in Birdfonts Overview window. How do I convert a BF file into a TTF, OTF, EOT, or SVG file? To export a BF file as a TTF, OTF, EOT, or SVG file, open the file in the paid version of Birdfont and select the sandwich menu. Then, select Import and Export → Export Fonts. Mac Birdfont. Windows Birdfont. Linux Birdfont. A BF file is a game data archive saved in the BigFile format, which is used by games developed by Ubisoft that use the LyN or Jade engine. It contains the majority of the data for the game, which may include objects, skins, maps, sounds, movies, and music. Some games that utilize the LyN or Jade engines are The Adventures of Tintin: The Game, Rabbids Go Home, From Dust, Just Dance 2, ZombiU, and Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time. BF files are not meant to be manually opened. Instead, they are referenced by the game to load gameplay content. However, users looking to modify the content in BF game archives can use custom scripts with QuickBMS to extract the contents in a BF archive. Windows QuickBMSFree.",
    "Windows XpoZeds Unpakke. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Windows bfbuilder. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Linux Vim. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Web Brainf*ck Interpreter. Android Brainf*ck Interpreter. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS. Mac Birdfont. Windows Birdfont. Linux Birdfont. Windows QuickBMS.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".ASSTRM",
    "Splinter Cell Blacklist Game Data File",
    "2.6",
    "Data file created for Splinter Cell Blacklist, a third-person shooter stealth game; accompanies.ASS files; contains gameplay data referenced by the game for each level in Splinter Cell; not meant to be manually opened.  Blacklist.asstrm - Included in all Splinter Cell Blacklist games. Windows Ubisoft Splinter Cell Blacklist.",
    "Windows Ubisoft Splinter Cell Blacklist.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".3GX",
    "Luma3DS 3GX Plug-in",
    "2.6",
    "A 3GX file is a Luma3DS 3GX (3DS Game eXtension) plug-in used by a Nintendo 3DS (N3DS) handheld gaming console with the Boot9Strap custom firmware loader and Luma3DS program installed. The file contains a plug-in that extends the functionality of an N3DS game, such as adding a cheat loader or game mod. You will most likely only encounter a 3GX file if you are an N3DS gamer looking to modify your games. The Luma3DS 3GX plug-in format is developed by Nanquitas and evolved from the NTR PLG plug-in format. The primary advancement is the ability to load C/C++/asm code into an N3DS game at runtime, which is then executed. You may create your own 3GX plug-in or download a plug-in and install it on your N3DS console (Boot9Strap must be installed) via an SD card. Luma3DS, which is a custom firmware program, must also be installed on your device. How do I install the 3GX plug-in? In order to install the 3GX plug-in, follow these instructions: Download the boot.firm file from here and place it in your SD card root to overwrite the current one. Create a plugins folder in the luma folder in your SD card. Make a folder with the name of the games titleid and place it in the plugins folder. Place the 3GX file in the folder with your game titleid. Insert the SD card in your 3DS device and boot it up (select Show NAND or user string in System Settings if you are greeted with a luma config screen, then press start). Open the rosalina menu in the home menu and enable the plug-in loader, then press B to exit rosalina. Open the game (the screen should flash green or blue when starting). 3GX files are not meant to be opened on your computer. Instead, you can load 3GX files with Luma3DS on a Nintendo 3DS gaming console that has Boot9Strap installed. No programs available.",
    "No programs available.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".VMAP",
    "Valve Source 2 Uncompiled Map File",
    "2.6",
    "A VMAP file is a map file created by the Valve Hammer Editor, a tool included with the Source SDK and used to create maps for games using the Source 2 engine. It contains a map, which may include lanes, ancients, fountains, barracks, runes, shops, neutral camps, towers, and other map elements. VMAP files are compiled into binary.VMAP_C files, which are then used in a game using the Source 2 engine. VMAP files are typically seen only by DOTA 2 gamers who want to modify playable maps. VMAP files were introduced with the release of the Source 2 engine and replaced.VMF files, which are used by games with the Source 1 engine. VMAP files are most commonly used by DOTA 2 but may also be used for other games that use the Source 2 engine. You can create and edit VMAP files with the Valve Hammer Editor, which is included in the Source SDK and DOTA 2 Workshop Tools. After you are done modifying a VMAP file, you must build it into a compiled map (VMAP_C file), which is packaged in a.VPK file. Select File → Build Map, choose your settings, and click Build to compile the VMAP file. Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Valve DOTA 2 Workshop ToolsFree.",
    "Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Valve DOTA 2 Workshop Tools.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".SV4",
    "RollerCoaster Tycoon Saved Game",
    "2.6",
    "Save file used by RollerCoaster Tycoon, a roller coaster creation game that allows users to manage amusement parks; contains saved game progress, which includes custom parks and themes from different locations and time periods across the world. NOTE: SV6 files can be manually edited with the RCT Saved Game Modifier (RCTSGM.exe). Windows Chris Sawyer RollerCoaster Tycoon.",
    "Windows Chris Sawyer RollerCoaster Tycoon.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".YDD",
    "Grand Theft Auto V 3D Character Model",
    "2.6",
    "A YDD file is a 3D model used in Grand Theft Auto V, an open-world action-adventure game published by Rockstar Games. It contains a character feature, such as a head, facial feature, hair, or article of clothing. YDD files are similar to.YDR files, which contain Grand Theft Auto V 3D objects. Modders use the OpenIV modding utility to extract YDD files from Grand Theft Auto V. Like YDR files, YDD files are compressed with Zlib compression. They can be decompressed to access the de-textured 3D model (.odd file) and textures stored in them. After extracting a YDD file from Grand Theft Auto V, GTA V modders can open the file in AutoDesk 3DS Max using the player-created GIMS Evo plug-in. They can then modify the file as they see fit before exporting it and loading it into GTA V using OpenIV. For more complete instructions, refer to this YouTube video. Windows AutoDesk 3DS Max with GIMS Evo plug-in installed. OpenIV. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto V.",
    "Windows AutoDesk 3DS Max with GIMS Evo plug-in installed. OpenIV. Rockstar Games Grand Theft Auto V.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BUS",
    "VirtualBus Board Parameters File",
    "2.6",
    "File created by OMSI The Bus Simulator, an omnibus driving simulator; contains configuration data for buses that appear during gameplay, such as speed and appearance; similar to other OMSI configuration files like.HUM,.SLI,.SCO, and.OVH files; can be customized. The BUS file is made up of lines of data following a keyword (whether its for a script or description). The format looks like this: [keyword] 1 2 3 OMSI will only read lines of data that are in this format. Windows MR Software OMSI The Bus Simulator 2. Configuration file used by VirtualBus, a free bus driving simulation game; saves parameters for bus boards, which are the active displays that animate bus route information on the front, back, and sides of the bus; can be edited with other bus package files to create custom buses. The BUS file for a bus package is named wysw.bus, and it is located in the same directory as other bus display configuration files, which include a.TS1 texture description file and bitmap (.BMP) graphics files. Windows VirtualBusFree.",
    "Windows MR Software OMSI The Bus Simulator 2. Windows VirtualBus.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".PBN",
    "Portable Bridge Notation File",
    "2.6",
    "Game file created in the Portable Bridge Notation (PBN) format, a standard format used for storing data for the card game Bridge; can save the results of a game as well as specify rules for dealing, bidding, playing, and teaching; allows data from one bridge game to be used in another game. The PBN format is based on the Portable Game Notation (PGN) format, which is used for chess games. Windows EasyBridge. WBridge5. RoboBridge. BridgeVu —  (Discontinued). Any text editor.",
    "Windows EasyBridge. WBridge5. RoboBridge. BridgeVu —  (Discontinued). Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".SCN",
    "SimCity 2000 Scenario",
    "2.5",
    "Game file used by OpenTTD, the open source follow-on project to Transport Tycoon; saves a game scenario, which defines the starting conditions for a map played by the user; may include the landscape, buildings, cities, train tracks, and other features. NOTE: SCN files are also used by the original Transport Tycoon. Windows OpenTTD. Microprose Transport Tycoon. An SCN file is a scenario file used by Age of Empires, Age of Empires II, or Age of Mythology, which are real-time strategy games developed by Microsoft. It contains a scenario map and a list of players starting units, players starting positions, and the scenarios victory conditions. Multiple SCN files can be combined into.CPN (Age of Empires / Mythology Campaign) files. Age of Empires and Age of Mythology are real-time strategy games in which players attempt to conquer rival cities and civilizations. Both games allow players to create and play scenarios that have specialized start and victory conditions. These scenarios are saved as SCN files. Multiple scenarios can be linked together into a campaign, which is saved as a CPN file. Age of Empires, Age of Empires II, and Age of Mythology players often share CPN and SCN files with each other, so they can play each others custom scenarios and campaigns. How do I create an Age of Empires / Mythology scenario? To create your own Age of Empires / Mythology scenarios, use the games Scenario Editors, which are accessible from the games main menus. In Age of Empires, the Scenario Editor is called the Scenario Builder. In Age of Empires II, the Scenario Editor is called the Map Editor. In Age of Mythology, the Scenario Editor is called Editor. You can open SCN files in Microsoft Age of Mythology, Age of Empires, and Age of Empires II (Windows) and use them as in-game scenarios. To open an SCN file, you must place the file in your games Scenario directory. Then, you will be able to select the scenario your SCN file describes in-game. Note that, if your scenario references custom animations, sounds, or images, you must also place those files in the correct game folders. How do I link multiple Age of Empires / Mythology scenarios into a campaign? If you want to link multiple SCN files into a single CPN file, you can do so using the CPNBuild command-line utility (Windows). CPNBuild allows players to add scenarios to campaigns, remove scenarios from campaigns, and extract scenarios from campaigns for use in other campaigns. Windows Microsoft Age of Empires. Microsoft Age of Empires 2. Microsoft Age of Mythology. Microsoft Age of Mythology: The Titans Expansion. CPNBUILDFree. An SCN file contains a scene created by Godot Engine, a free and open source game engine used to create 2D and 3D games. It stores binary data about a single scene tree inside Godot Engine, which includes paths to any external resources, and information about internal resources, connections, and nodes. To open a scene in a SCN file in Godot Engine, select Scene → Open Scene.. or Open Recent. To create a scene and save it as a SCN file in Godot Engine, select Scene → New Scene or New Inherited Scene.. Then, select Scene → Save Scene or Save Scene As... Mac Godot Engine. Windows Godot Engine. Linux Godot EngineFree. An SCN file is a scenario that can be loaded in SimCity 2000, a popular city-building video game. It includes a starter city and specialized rules that define the scenario. SimCity 2000 contains 18 official SCN files, used to load the games 18 included scenarios. In SimCity 2000, players act as a hybrid mayor/urban planner who must shepherd a city to success. Players can design their own cities in the games free-play mode, or they can attempt to complete one of the games specialized scenarios. Each scenario includes a starter city, often modeled on a real-world city, challenging circumstances the player must overcome, and one or more victory conditions. If the player completes the scenario, the citys residents name the player mayor, and the player can continue playing in free-play mode. Scenarios are saved as SCN files. SimCity 2000 contains 18 official SCN files. Additionally, custom SCN files, created by SimCity 2000 modders, are available for download online. You can open an SCN file in SimCity 2000 (Windows, Mac). To do so, place the file in the games Scenario directory. Then, open the game and select File → Load Scenario to load your SCN file. Mac Maxis SimCity 2000. Windows Maxis SimCity 2000. Contains information about multiple scenes within a single video file; used by Pinnacle Studio to describe scenes and to specify when they begin and end; typically saved along with an.AVI file with the same filename. SCN files can also be opened by Paul Glaglas DVdate and ImageGrab programs. Windows Pinnacle Studio. DVdate ImageGrab. An SCN file is a slide specimen image created by a Leica Microsystems microscope or other slide scanning device. It contains a collection of TIFF images, and its ImageDescription tag contains an XML document that defines the slides structure. SCN files also contain metadata specifying the device that created the file (leica.device-model and leica.device-version), the date the file was created (leica.creation-date), and the aperture, illumination source, and objective of the files main image (leica.aperture, leica.illumination-source, and leica.objective). Scientific microscopes scan and save slide specimen images in a variety of image formats. Some Leica microscopes save images in the SCN file format, which contains a number of different specimen images saved at different sizes and resolutions. Programs that can open SCN files combine the various images the file contains into one image, which can be zoomed in and out upon. In this way, scientists can view the specimen a slide contains at various resolutions in slide viewing software. Windows users can open SCN files (Leica Whole Slide Images) in Aperio Technologies ImageScope, OpenSlide, ImageJ, or NetScope Viewer. Mac and Linux users can open SCN files in OpenSlide or ImageJ. Mac OpenSlide. ImageJ. Windows Aperio Technologies ImageScope. OpenSlide. ImageJ. NetScope Viewer. Linux OpenSlide. ImageJFree. Data file used by Orbiter, a free space browsing and simulation program; used for creating automated space simulations; includes information about the space scraft, the space travel route, camera angles, and the space environment; saved in a plain text format. Windows OrbiterFree. Image file created by TreePaint Plus, a program used to create print designs for photoengraving, silk-screen processes, and other types of print mediums; supports 256 color, 65,536 color, or 24-bit true color formats; may contain colorway and silk-screen separation information; used for textile and fashion solutions. Windows TreePaint Plus. An SCN file is a data file created by TD Scan, a software suite used to view, analyze, and create reports of ultrasonic data. It contains a scan of ultrasonic data from industrial components such as pipeline welds, forgings and castings, and pressure vessels welds. TD Scan is used for monitoring and analyzing the performance industrial facilities such as nuclear power plants. It offers real-time data collection, video tracking, and Time-of-Flight-Diffraction (ToFD), Pulse Echo, and corrosion mapping capabilities. The program stores scans in the SCN file, which is used for complete scans or for split scans that can be joined together when the data size becomes too large. NOTE: To open an SCN file in TD Scan, select File → Open Scan File. Windows Technology Design TD Scan. An SCN file is an image created by a Bio-Rad gel imaging system. It contains a digital copy of a gel electrophoresis result. SCN files are used to analyze results and share them with other Bio-Rad users. Biochemists use Bio-Rad gel imaging systems to record and analyze the results of gel electrophoresis tests. For example, a biochemist may use a Bio-Rad system to record and analyze the result of a western blot, which is a test that detects specific proteins in a tissue sample. Bio-Rad systems save copies of biochemists electrophoresis results as SCN images. You can open an SCN file (Bio-Rad Gel Image) in Bio-Rad Image Lab (Windows, Mac). The standard version of Image Lab can be downloaded for free from Bio-Rads website, after you register for a Bio-Rad account. Those who do not want to register for a Bio-Lab account can use ImageJ and its accompanying Bio-Formats library (cross-platform) to view SCN images. Mac Bio-Rad Image Lab. ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Windows Bio-Rad Image Lab. ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Linux ImageJ with Bio-Formats libraryFree.",
    "Windows OpenTTD. Microprose Transport Tycoon. Windows Microsoft Age of Empires. Microsoft Age of Empires 2. Microsoft Age of Mythology. Microsoft Age of Mythology: The Titans Expansion. CPNBUILD. Mac Godot Engine. Windows Godot Engine. Linux Godot Engine. Mac Maxis SimCity 2000. Windows Maxis SimCity 2000. Windows Pinnacle Studio. DVdate ImageGrab. Mac OpenSlide. ImageJ. Windows Aperio Technologies ImageScope. OpenSlide. ImageJ. NetScope Viewer. Linux OpenSlide. ImageJ. Windows Orbiter. Windows TreePaint Plus. Windows Technology Design TD Scan. Mac Bio-Rad Image Lab. ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Windows Bio-Rad Image Lab. ImageJ with Bio-Formats library. Linux ImageJ with Bio-Formats library.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".SMO",
    "Sumotori Dreams Arena File",
    "2.5",
    "Game file used by Sumotori Dreams, a game that simulates rag doll wrestlers; contains properties for an arena that the dolls wrestle within; used for both custom game arenas, called mods, as well as the default arenas installed with the game. You can load SMO files in Sumotori Dreams by choosing the Play Mod button from the start screen. Windows Gravitysensation.com Sumotori Dreams.",
    "Windows Gravitysensation.com Sumotori Dreams.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".WX",
    "Flight Simulator Weather File",
    "2.5",
    "A WX file is a backup file created by Wanam Xposed, a module for the Xposed Framework featured in Samsung devices that run Android 4.2 or later. The file contains a backup of the apps theme profile, which can be imported into the app. The Wanama Xposed application enables you to customize a large amount of options on your Samsung device. You can change the appearance of the clock, battery, and date displays, and the notification bar. You can also add other capabilities such as recovery and download mode options and the ability to kill apps with a long-press of the volume down button. Android Wanam Xposed —  (Discontinued). Stores weather conditions for a flight created with Microsoft Flight Simulator; may be customized by clicking the World menu, then Weather within the Flight Simulator program; weather settings may be modified using the Clouds, Precipitation, Visibility, and Wind sliders; can be customized more specifically using the Advanced Weather Settings. The WX file is saved along with the.FLT file when creating a flight. NOTE: WX files are used by multiple versions of Flight Simulator, including Flight Simulator 2004 and Flight Simulator X. Mac Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition.",
    "Android Wanam Xposed —  (Discontinued). Mac Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition. Windows Microsoft Flight Simulator X Steam Edition.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".DEH",
    "DeHackEd Patch",
    "2.5",
    "A DEH file is a patch that can be applied to the original version of Doom using DeHackEd, a DOS-based Doom editor. It contains binary or text data that is used to modify Dooms gameplay. DEH files are now most commonly used to create custom.WAD files, which are also used to modify Doom. Doom is a popular first-person shooter video game that was released in 1993. In Dooms infancy, developer Greg Lewis created the DeHackEd editor, which allowed players to modify Dooms gameplay. DeHackEd users created patches, saved in DEH files, that they then applied to Dooms executable file. This created a custom executable named doomhack.exe, which players could launch to play their custom version of Doom. Over the years, Doom modders have developed easier and more flexible methods of modifying Dooms gameplay. As a result, most current Doom modders do not use DeHackEd or DEH files. However, some modders continue to enjoy the challenge and nostalgia of using DEH-based mods, so some Doom modding programs still support DEH files. For example, the GZDoom modding platform allows players to import DEH files and save them as custom WAD files. The easiest way to use a DEH file as a Doom mod is to save it as part of a custom WAD file. You can load a DEH file and save it as part of a WAD file in GZDoom (cross-platform) and SLADE (cross-platform). After youve created your custom WAD file, you can use GZDoom to apply the file to Doom. If you need to modify a DEH file, you can do so using WhackEd4 (Windows). Windows DeHackEd —  (Discontinued). WhackEd4. ZDoom. GZDoom. SLADE. Mac GZDoom. SLADE. Linux GZDoom. SLADEFree.",
    "Windows DeHackEd —  (Discontinued). WhackEd4. ZDoom. GZDoom. SLADE. Mac GZDoom. SLADE. Linux GZDoom. SLADE.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".RCF",
    "Radical Cement File",
    "2.5",
    "Configuration file used by SoniCWALL Global VPN Client, a program that allows client workstations to connect to a Virtual Private Network (VPN); saved using XML formatting and contains connection information for one or more VPNs; used by organizations for setting up remote connections for employees. Windows SonicWALL Global VPN ClientFree. An RCF file is an archive that contains data used by a Radical Entertainment video game, such as Prototype. RCF archives contain in-game character models, as well as other data. Radical Entertainment was a Canadian video game development company that developed several popular games, including some games in the Crash Bandicoot series. In 2009, Radical Entertainment released Prototype, an open-world action-adventure video game. Prototype stores some of its game data in archives that use the.rcf extension. These archives contain various game data, including 3D models and related textures used to show in-game objects and characters. RCF files are not meant to be manually opened. To see the game data an RCF file contains, you must play Prototype. Windows Radical Entertainment Prototype. An RCF file is a remote control configuration file used by RCoid Remote Control, an Android app that allows users to use their smartphone in place of a devices remote control. It contains data that RCoid uses to mimic a devices remote control, including the controls layout and functions. RCoid users can download RCF files at https://www.rcoid.de/remotesuche.php. RCoid allows an Android user to turn their smartphone into a universal remote control, capable of controlling many different electronic devices. For example, an RCoid user could install remotes for their television, soundbar, and DVD player, allowing them to control their entire home theater system from their smartphone. The remote configuration files that RCoid uses to load remote layouts and pair with an associated device are saved as RCF files. Many RCF files are available for download on RCoids website, organized alphabetically by electronics brand name. You can open an RCF file in RCoid Remote Control for Android. The program is available in both free and paid versions, either of which can be used to load the remote configuration an RCF file contains. Android RCoid Remote Control Free. RCoid Remote Control ProFree.",
    "Windows SonicWALL Global VPN Client. Windows Radical Entertainment Prototype. Android RCoid Remote Control. RCoid Remote Control Pro.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".PAT0",
    "Wii Texture Pattern File ",
    "2.5",
    "Pattern file used by Nintendo Wii games such as Super Smash Bros. Brawl and Mario Kart; contains texture patterns referenced by the game to create animations; often found within a.BRRES resource package file; similar to.MDL0 and.PLT0 files. PAT0 files are referenced by the game to determine what your 3D model looks like with a looping animation. The PAT0 file communicates what.TEX0 texture files overlay your 3D model and the amount of frames per second you want the textures to appear on your model. NOTE: The BrawlBox application enables you to open BRRES files and the contained PAT0 files, as well. Windows BrawlBoxFree.",
    "Windows BrawlBox.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BCRES",
    "Nintendo 3DS Game Model",
    "2.5",
    "A BCRES file is a game data file used by a Nintendo 3DS video game. It contains an in-game model as well as related textures, animations, and camera data. BCRES files are used in several popular 3DS games, including Animal Crossing: New Leaf and New Super Mario Bros. 2. Nintendo video games use a variety of proprietary file formats to store game data. Some Nintendo 3DS games store in-game character, item, and terrain models and related files in BCRES files. Most gamers will never encounter BCRES files, except those who want to mod the assets BCRES files contain. A variety of player-made utilities allow 3DS gamers to open BCRES files and export the data they contain in common file formats, such as.OBJ,.DAE, and.PNG. These utilities include Ohana3DS Rebirth (Windows), SPICA (Windows), and EveryFileExplorer (Windows). Windows Ohana3DS Rebirth. SPICA. EveryFileExplorer. Switch-ToolboxFree.",
    "Windows Ohana3DS Rebirth. SPICA. EveryFileExplorer. Switch-Toolbox.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".DA5",
    "AGT Game Data File",
    "2.5",
    "Game data file referenced by AGiliTy, a program that interprets Adventure Game Toolkit (AGT) games; contains meta-language commands for the game, which are conditional tests that help the game determine if an action made by the player is possible; will not exist if there are no meta-language commands in the game. In order to navigate through Interactive fiction games, like AGT games, you must type commands in the game. The story will change depending on what decisions you type. There are several files that are packaged with AGT games. These files contain game data and include.INS,.TTL, and.VOC files. Since there is a large amount of files that accompany the AGT game, the AGT2AGX utility that comes with AGiliTy can convert the data files into a single.AGX file. This conversion reduces clutter, load time, and game size. NOTE: The DA5 file is similar to the.DA3,.DA4, and.DA6 file. These files contain game data referenced for different aspects of the game. [name of the game].da5 - The DA5 file possesses the same name as the game its created for. Windows AGiliTyFree.",
    "Windows AGiliTy.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BARS",
    "Binary Sound Archive",
    "2.5",
    "A BARS file contains audio used by a Nintendo Wii U or Switch video game. It may be saved as a.SARC archive, or it may be saved as a chunked file. Games created before The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild use BARS files saved as archives; BOTW and later games use chunked BARS files. BARS files store audio saved in the.BFSTM,.BFWAV, or.BWAV formats. These audio files are used to play in-game music, sound effects, and dialogue. While BARS files are not meant to be opened by players, players have created utilities that allow them to extract the audio BARS files contain. Examples of games that use BARS files include: Splatoon Super Mario Maker The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild Animal Crossing: New Horizons. You can use BARS to BWAV (multiplatform) to extract BWAV files from Nintendo Switch BARS files. For example, you can use BARS to BWAV to extract BWAV files from Animal Crossing: New Horizons BARS files. You can also use VGMToolbox (Windows) to extract audio from newer BARS files and SARCTools (Windows) to extract audio from older BARS files. You may also be able to play the audio a BARS file contains using Nullsoft Winamp, with the vgmstream plug-in installed. Windows BARS to BWAV. VGMToolbox. SARCTools. Nullsoft Winamp with vgmstream plug-in. Mac BARS to BWAV. Linux BARS to BWAVFree.",
    "Windows BARS to BWAV. VGMToolbox. SARCTools. Nullsoft Winamp with vgmstream plug-in. Mac BARS to BWAV. Linux BARS to BWAV.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".TOC",
    "World of Warcraft Add-on Table of Contents File",
    "2.5",
    "A TOC file is an audio file saved in a format compatible with the PlayStation Portable (PSP). It likely contains a song that has been converted to the TOC format for use with Grand Theft Auto: Liberty City Stories or Grand Theft Auto: Vice City Stories. Using the app Exact Audio Copy (EAC), players can import TOC files into these games. Like other audio files created for use on the PSP, TOC files are saved using Adaptive Transform Acoustic Coding (ATRAC) compression. In this way, they are similar to.AA3 and.ATRAC files. To create TOC files, gamers use EAC or a related program, named Rockstar Custom Tracks, to convert.MP3 files to TOC files. They then save their TOC files to a custom tracks sub-directory found within a games SAVEDATA directory. (To do this, a gamer must connect their PSPs removable storage to their computer.). To use a TOC file with Grand Theft Auto: Liberty City Stories or Grand Theft Auto: Vice City Stories: Place the file in either the ULES00182CUSTOMTRACKS (GTA: LCS) or ULES00503CUSTOMTRACKS (GTA: VCS) directory on your PSPs removable storage (found within the PSP/​SAVEDATA directory). Replace your PSPs removable storage. Play the game whose data you modified. In the games Pause menu, select Audio → My songs ON. You can then listen to the audio your TOC file contains on the in-game radio, while driving vehicles. Windows Exact Audio Copy —  (Discontinued). Contains a table of contents for messages stored within a certain Eudora mail folder; lists all the messages that are displayed when a mail folder is opened within Eudora. NOTE: Eudora is no longer actively developed. in.toc - Inbox table of contents out.toc - Outbox table of contents junk.toc - Junkmail table of contents trash.toc - Trash table of contents. Mac QUALCOMM Eudora. Windows QUALCOMM EudoraFree. Data file created by Brasero, a disc authoring program for Unix; defines the table of contents (or structure) of the data stored within a disc image; saved along with a corresponding.BIN file, which contains the actual data. NOTE: Both the TOC and BIN files are required to burn a disc image to a CD or DVD with Brasero. Linux BraseroFree. File used by World of Warcraft, a massively multiplayer online role-playing game (MMORPG); contains table of contents information for a user interface add-on; used to describe the add-on name, description, saved variables, and instructions for how the add-on should be loaded. TOC files contain lines of text with ## tags followed by a series filenames. First, tags describe information for the client. For example, ## Version: 1.2 may provide the add-on version. Second, a list of filenames describes the order in which the add-on files are loaded. NOTE: TOC files often reference Blizzard Texture files (.LUA) and.XML configuration files. Mac Blizzard World of Warcraft. Blizzard World of Warcraft Interface AddOn Kit. Windows Blizzard World of Warcraft. Blizzard World of Warcraft Interface AddOn Kit. Addon Studio for World of Warcraft.",
    "Windows Exact Audio Copy —  (Discontinued). Mac QUALCOMM Eudora. Windows QUALCOMM Eudora. Linux Brasero. Mac Blizzard World of Warcraft. Blizzard World of Warcraft Interface AddOn Kit. Windows Blizzard World of Warcraft. Blizzard World of Warcraft Interface AddOn Kit. Addon Studio for World of Warcraft.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".FFD",
    "FATE Saved Game",
    "2.5",
    "An FFD file is a game save created by FATE, an action-adventure role-playing game published by WildTangent. It contains a record of a players progress, including the players items and character stats. Players use FFD files to resume their saved games. FATE is a single-player dungeon crawler in which players fight monsters, complete quests, and collect items in procedurally-generated dungeons. WildTangent released FATE in 2005. When a FATE player saves their game, the game creates a corresponding FFD file. FFD files are numbered in the order they were created. For example, a players first saved game will be named 0.ffd, the second 1.ffd, and so on. FATE typically stores FFD files in the games SAVE directory. You can use an FFD file to resume the saved game it contains in FATE (Windows). To do so, first place the file in FATEs SAVE directory. Then, open FATE, select Continue Game, and select the saved game your FFD file contains. You can also use various FFD editing tools, such as FATE Save Editor, to modify the save data an FFD file contains. For example, FATE Save Editor allows you to edit your characters stats, skills, items, and spells. Windows WildTangent FATE. FATE Save EditorFree. Video project file created by ffDiaporama a program used for making video sequences; may include video clips, images, audio, and transitions; used for saving and loading editing projects. NOTE: FFD files do not store actual audio or video files. Instead, they contain file references. Therefore, to transfer a project between computers, make sure to copy the audio and video files as well. Windows ffDiaporama. Linux ffDiaporamaFree. File format developed by Contivo (now Liaison Technologies); similar to an.XSLT file but defines transformation rules for mapping non-XML binary data into an XML dataset; saved in an XML format and can be created using a text editor or an IDE such as Liaison Technologies Analyst. FFD files are also used for XML translation by IBMs WebSphere DataPower SOA (Service Oriented Architecture) appliances. The application is no longer available. Windows Liaison Technologies Analyst. Log file generated by FFDDumper, a Microsoft SharePoint Server program used for debugging document search results; saved in a plain text format and contains the results of a document being crawled by SharePoints FAST document processing engine. FFD files help administrators examine low-level document properties so they can debug why certain searches provide certain results. Windows Microsoft SharePoint. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "Windows WildTangent FATE. FATE Save Editor. Windows ffDiaporama. Linux ffDiaporama. Windows Liaison Technologies Analyst. Windows Microsoft SharePoint. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".S10",
    "Brasfoot Saved Game File",
    "2.5",
    "Saved state created by Brasfoot 2010, a game where players coach and manage soccer teams; stores the state of the soccer players, leagues, and stadiums; used to save and load progress during an in-game soccer season. Brasfoot saved game files use the extensions .sXX where XX is the two-digit year that corresponds to the version of the game. For example, Brasfoot 2005 saved games use the .s05 extension. Yearly versions of the game have been released since 2004. NOTE: Brasfoot was created for the Portuguese language. Windows Brasfoot.",
    "Windows Brasfoot.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".FRC",
    "FS Recorder File",
    "2.5",
    "Color settings file created by Mandelbrot Explorer, a visualization program for Mandelbrot Set and Julia Set fractal images; stores a color scheme that can be overlaid onto a generated fractal graphic; supports black and white, grayscale, and color patterns. NOTE: FRC files were replaced by.MXCS files after Mandelbrot Explorer 2.5. Windows Mandelbrot ExplorerFree. Recording of a Flight Simulator flight created with FS Recorder, an add-on module for Microsoft Flight Simulator; can be played back with multiple views and may include AI traffic. FRC files may be generated within Flight Simulator 2004 as well as Flight Simulator X (FSX). Windows FS Recorder —  (Discontinued). FRC Editor ConvertIt RecorderToolBox.",
    "Windows Mandelbrot Explorer. Windows FS Recorder —  (Discontinued). FRC Editor ConvertIt RecorderToolBox.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".ARKTRIBE",
    "ARK: Survival Evolved Tribe File",
    "2.5",
    "An ARKTRIBE file contains a player profile saved by ARK: Survival Evolved, an action-adventure survival game. It stores information about a tribe, which includes the IDs and names of players in the tribe, the level of the tribe, and the name and ID of the tribe owner. The ARKTRIBE file is one of 3 save files that ARK: Survival Evolved gamers commonly encounter. The.ARK file contains information about a world and the.ARKPROFILE file contains information about a player profile. ARKTRIBE files are saved by default by Steam installations of ARK: Survival Evolved in the following Windows directory: C:/​Program Files (x86)/​Steam/​steamapps/​common/​ARK/​ShooterGame/​Saved/​SavedArksLocal/​. [TribeID].arktribe - The name given to ARKTRIBE files is the ID of the tribe. Windows Studio Wildcard ARK: Survival Evolved.",
    "Windows Studio Wildcard ARK: Survival Evolved.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".DSI",
    "Nintendo DSiware Game ROM",
    "2.5",
    "File created by DAZ Studio, a program used for 3D character modeling; stores multiple image layers as a material file that can be applied to 3D objects; allows the source images (e.g.,.PNG or.JPG) to be combined while allowing each image to remain unmodified from its original state. Windows DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Mac DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4Free. A DSI file is an official Nintendo DSi game ROM issued by Nintendo. It contains a game downloaded from the Nintendo DSi Shop. DSI files can be used to play games on the Nintendo DSi and Nintendo 3DS, as well as in Nintendo DSi and 3DS emulators. The Nintendo DSi was the successor to the Nintendo DS and the predecessor to the Nintendo 3DS. The DSi and the 3DS allowed gamers to download a collection of games, commonly referred to as DSiWare, from the Nintendo DSi Shop and eShop. DSiWare games were saved in DSI files. In addition to allowing players to play downloaded games on their Nintendo devices, DSI files can be used to create unofficial ROMs that PC-based DSi and 3DS emulators, such as Citra, can open. To create an emulator-compatible ROM from a DSI file, gamers can use GodMode9 (Nintendo 3DS) or GodMode9i (Nintendo DSi). You can use GodMode9 (Nintendo 3DS) or GodMode9i (Nintendo DSi) to transform a DSI file into a Citra-compatible ROM. Then, you can use your new ROM to play the game your DSI file contains in Citra (cross-platform). Windows Citra. Mac Citra. Linux Citra. Android CitraFree. 3D image file created by Fryrender, a physics-based light simulator application used for photo-realistic rendering; stores a spectral map, which stores the radiances captured by the camera; used in the process of rendering the final lighting effects onto an image. DSI files are generated from a source.FRY scene file. NOTE: fryrender has been discontinued. Windows RandomControl fryrender.",
    "Windows DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Mac DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Windows Citra. Mac Citra. Linux Citra. Android Citra. Windows RandomControl fryrender.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".PPM",
    "Flipnote Studio Animation",
    "2.5",
    "A PPM file is a raster image saved in the Portable Pixmap format. It contains plain text that specifies the images type (plain or raw), its number of columns and rows, and its maximum color value. Plain PPM files then specify each pixels color using ASCII-encoded numbers, while raw PPM files specify each included pixels color using raw binary data. PPM file open in XnViewMP In the late 1980s, developer Jef Poskanzer created the PPM image format and added tools that could create and read PPM images to Pbmplus, his library of tools used to create and manage.PBM,.PGM, and PPM images. PPM files contain color images saved using an RGB color model. Typically, the images use a 24-bit color depth. In most PPM files, each pixels color is specified using a trio of ASCII numbers that set the pixels red, green, and blue color values. Image rows are comprised of sets of RGB values equal to the images width. These types of PPM files are referred to as plain PPM files and can be identified by the magic number P3 in their header. Raw PPM files, on the other hand, specify each pixels color using raw binary data, instead of ASCII-encoded numbers. If you were to open a raw PPM file in a text editor, its body would appear as gibberish instead of an understandable series of numbers. These files include the magic number P6 in their header. While many programs support the PPM format, PPM images have quite large file sizes when compared with images saved in other formats, because they are not compressed. Thus, the PPM format is not used much. You can open a PPM file with many image viewing and editing programs. For example, you can open a PPM file with GIMP (multiplatform), XnViewMP (multiplatform), or Netpbm (multiplatform). Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus. GIMP. ImageMagick. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. ImageMagick. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Android File Viewer for Android. Data file used to flash some Nokia mobile phones; sometimes used to change the language pack on a phone to support a different language; may also use the.PPM_B, PPM_C, or PPM_D file extensions. Windows BB5 FLS Editor. A PPM file is an animation created by Flipnote Studio, a free animation app available for the Nintendo DSi. It contains animation frames and audio. PPM files are typically stored on a Nintendo DSi SD card. Flipnote Studio is an animation app that Nintendo DSi players can download from the DSi Shop. It allows gamers to create simple animations and save them to their DSIs SD cards. These animations are saved as PPM files. PPM files are typically stored in the following locations: North America: /​private/​ds/​app/​4B475545/​001 Europe: /​private/​ds/​app/​4B475556/​001 Some players have uploaded their PPM files to online Flipnote repositories, such as Flipnote Hatena or PPM Archive, from which other Flipnote users can download them. NOTE: The PPM extension comes from Flipnote Studios in-development name, Para Para Manga Koubou. In addition to being able to open and play PPM files in Flipnote Studio, you can open them in the web-based Flipnote Player. Web Flipnote PlayerFree.",
    "Web File Helper. Windows File Viewer Plus. GIMP. ImageMagick. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. GIMP. ImageMagick. Adobe Photoshop with CartaPGM plugin. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Linux GIMP. ImageMagick. Netpbm. LibreOffice. qView. Android File Viewer for Android. Windows BB5 FLS Editor. Web Flipnote Player.",
    "You can use Netpbm, ImageMagick or XnViewMP to convert PPM files to other image formats. For example, XnViewMP can convert PPM files to the following formats (and many others):.JPG - JPEG Image.GIF - Graphical Interchange Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format.BMP - Bitmap Image.PCX - Paintbrush Bitmap Image.TGA - Targa Graphic.JP2 - JPEG 2000 Core Image.JXR - JPEG XR Image.WEBP - WebP Image."],
    ["game_files",
    ".SUD",
    "Sudoku Puzzle File",
    "2.5",
    "Project saved by Super Project Analyzer, a program that analyzes software development projects; contains information about files, procedures, constants, variables, data types and enums. SUD files track file usage within a project. The program determines which files are necessary and which are not. Project elements are then labeled as Included, Shared, Used, or Dead.. Windows Aivosto Super Project Analyzer. Puzzle created for Sudoku software; contains numbers arranged in grids; may be opened by various Sudoku games and Sudoku puzzle solving programs; also used by some Java-based Sudoku applets available on the Web. Windows Pappocom Sudoku. Kojens Sudoku CAD Sudoku SolverFree.",
    "Windows Aivosto Super Project Analyzer. Windows Pappocom Sudoku. Kojens Sudoku CAD Sudoku Solver.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".RW4",
    "RenderWare 4 3D Model",
    "2.5",
    "An RW4 file is a 3D model file used in an Electronic Arts video game, such as Spore or SimCity (2013). It contains meshes, textures, lighting maps, and animations used to show a character or object in-game. RW4 files are found in.PACKAGE files. Some Electronic Arts video games released in the late 2000s and early 2010s use the RenderWare 4 graphics engine to load and show graphics to players. 3D models used by the RenderWare 4 graphics engine are saved as RW4 files. Most prominently, Spore and SimCity (2013) use the RenderWare 4 graphics engine. Modders of these games have created tools that allow them to open and examine RW4 files contents. You can open an RW4 file and examine some of its contents in the following modding tools: SporeModder FX (Windows) SporeMaster (Windows) SimCityPak (Windows) When opening an RW4 file, be sure to open it in a related modding tool. For example, open a Spore RW4 file in a Spore tool, and a SimCity RW4 file in a SimCity tool. Mac Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. Windows Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. SporeModder FX. SporeMaster. SimCityPakFree.",
    "Mac Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. Windows Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. SporeModder FX. SporeMaster. SimCityPak.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".HE0",
    "Humongous Entertainment Game Archive",
    "2.5",
    "Game resource file used by Humongous Entertainment games, such as Freddi Fish and the Putt Putt game series; contains game data that describes characters and places that appear in the game. HE0 files are archives used by adventure games, such as Putt-Putt, Fatty Bear, Pajama Sam, and Freddi Fish, developed by Humongous Entertainment to store game data. The HE0 file is also used by ScummVM, a reiteration of the SCUMM game engine that lets you play classic games on your current machine. NOTE: The HE0 resource file is located in the game directory. Windows ScummVM. Mac ScummVM. Linux ScummVMFree.",
    "Windows ScummVM. Mac ScummVM. Linux ScummVM.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".UNITYWEB",
    "Unity WebGL Game Data",
    "2.5",
    "A UNITYWEB file is a binary game data file used by a Unity WebGL video game. It contains either the games JavaScript runtime and plug-ins, the games WebAssembly, a binary image used to initialize the heap memory for the games player, or the games asset and scene data. UNITYWEB files may be compressed using gzip or Brotli compression, or they may be uncompressed, depending on how the developer who created the files chose to build their game. Unity is a cross-platform 3D video game development application. One of the platforms for which Unity developers can create games is WebGL. WebGL uses a JavaScript API to render 2D and 3D graphics in a web browser, allowing players to play Unity-developed games in a web browser. When a developer builds their game for WebGL, Unity produces a folder with a variety of files related to that game. Some of these files are UNITYWEB files. UNITYWEB files are located in a games Build directory, and they are named: MyProject.wasm.framework.unityweb: Contains the games JavaScript runtime and plug-ins MyProject.wasm.code.unityweb: Contains the games WebAssembly binary MyProject.wasm.memory.unityweb: Contains a binary image used to initialize the heap memory for the games player; generated only for multi-threaded builds MyProject.data.unityweb: Contains the games assets and scenes NOTE: Some Unity WebGL games may include additional UNITYWEB files in their Build directory, depending on which version of Unity was used to build the game. UNITYWEB files are not meant to be opened manually. However, modders and other developers who wish to extract assets from asset-related UNITYWEB files can do so using AssetStudio (Windows), the Unity Assets Bundle Extractor (Windows), and other Unity asset extraction tools. Windows Unity Technologies Unity. AssetStudio. Unity Assets Bundle Extractor. Mac Unity Technologies Unity. Linux Unity Technologies UnityFree.",
    "Windows Unity Technologies Unity. AssetStudio. Unity Assets Bundle Extractor. Mac Unity Technologies Unity. Linux Unity Technologies Unity.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".P2C",
    "Portal 2 Community Puzzle File",
    "2.5",
    "A P2C file contains a community, or co-operative, puzzle used by Portal 2, a first-person puzzle solving game. It stores the definition of puzzle in a voxel X Y Z (X is right, Y is forward, Z is up) format where each voxel represents a 1 x 1 x 1 panel area in the puzzle. P2C files also contain metadata about the puzzle, which includes the title, description, creation time, and version. P2C files are saved in plain text and can be opened and edited by a text editor. They can also be opened by the level editor included with Portal 2 and exported to the.VMF Valve Map file format. P2C files are located in the following directory: C:/​Program Files (x86)/​Steam/​steamapps/​common/​portal 2/​puzzles/​. Windows Valve Portal 2.",
    "Windows Valve Portal 2.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".SDFDATA",
    "Snowdrop Data File",
    "2.5",
    "An SDFDATA file is an archive included in a video game developed using the Ubisoft Snowdrop game engine. It contains assets (meshes, models, animations, textures, sounds, text) used in an Ubisoft video game. Tom Clancys The Division, Mario + Rabbids, and South Park: The Fractured But Whole all use SDFDATA files. Most players will never encounter an SDFDATA file. However, players who are interested in modding games developed using Snowdrop will likely want to extract assets from or repackage assets into the games SDFDATA files. NOTE: SDFDATA files are accompanied by an.SDFTOC file. Modders have developed a variety of tools that allow them to extract files from and repackage files into SDFDATA archives. For example, the rouge_sdf tool allows players to extract assets from The Divisions SDFDATA files. Windows rouge_sdf. Mac rouge_sdf. Linux rouge_sdfFree.",
    "Windows rouge_sdf. Mac rouge_sdf. Linux rouge_sdf.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BRCTR",
    "Binary Revolution Control File",
    "2.5",
    "A BRCTR file is a user interface control file for Mario Kart Wii and other Nintendo Wii video games. It uses the data stored in.BRLYT and.BRLAN files to show menus and menu animations to players. Mario Kart Wiis BRCTR files are stored in the games ctrl directories. BRCTR files contain references to the BRLYT files and BRLAN files they use to show user interface items to players. Some of the user interface items that BRCTR files control the appearance of include menu buttons, backgrounds, and layouts. You can open and edit BRCTR files in Wexoss Toolbox (Windows), a player-created Wii game asset editor. Windows Wexoss ToolboxFree.",
    "Windows Wexoss Toolbox.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".XP4",
    "KiriKiri Package",
    "2.5",
    "File used by KiriKiri, a Japanese visual novel scripting engine; may store text, images, audio, and other data used by a visual novel; used for packaging data together in a single compressed file for the story. Windows KiriKiri.",
    "Windows KiriKiri.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".PM",
    "Progressive Mesh",
    "2.5",
    "Bitmap image format generated by the Unix program xv, an interactive image manipulation program for the X Window System; also a used by IBMs OS/2 Presentation Manager. Windows XnViewMP. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Mac XnViewMP. Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. Linux xv. Module containing Perl functions that can be referenced and used by Perl programs; may be one of two different types:. 1) Traditional - defines subroutines and variables for the function referencing the module to import and use. 2) Object-oriented - functions as a class definition and is accessed through method calls. Some Perl modules may offer traditional and object-oriented functionality. Windows File Viewer Plus. Perl Express Open Perl IDE Solutionsoft Perl Builder Use and compile with Perl Edit with a text editor Mac MacroMates TextMate. Bare Bones BBEdit. Use and compile with Perl Edit with a text editor Linux Use and compile with Perl Edit with a text editor. A PM file is a 3D model used by legacy versions of Trainz Railroad Simulator. It contains data used to show a train car or other object in-game. The PM format was replaced by the.IM format. Trainz Railroad Simulator is a video game in which players simulate routing and operating trains. The first version of the game, titled simply Trainz, was released by Auran in 2001. The game has since received many sequels. It is now published by N3V Games. Previous versions of Trainz used 3D models saved in the PM format, or Progressive Mesh, format. This format supported a specialized, multi-faceted form of level of detail specification. However, advances in graphics technology rendered the PM format obsolete. Instead, Trainz began using IM, or Indexed Mesh, models, which contained a single level of detail specification. You can use PEVSoft Trainz Mesh Viewer 2 (Windows) to view the 3D model a PM file contains. There is no program that allows users to edit PM files. You can use PEVSoft PM2IM (Windows) to convert a PM file to the.IM (Indexed Mesh) format. This allows you to use the model your PM file contains with later versions of Trainz Railroad Simulator. Windows N3V Games Trainz Simulator. PEVSoft Trainz Mesh Viewer 2. PEVSoft PM2IMFree.",
    "Windows XnViewMP. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Mac XnViewMP. Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. Linux xv. Windows File Viewer Plus. Perl Express Open Perl IDE Solutionsoft Perl Builder Use and compile with Perl Edit with a text editor. Mac MacroMates TextMate. Bare Bones BBEdit. Use and compile with Perl Edit with a text editor. Linux Use and compile with Perl Edit with a text editor. Windows N3V Games Trainz Simulator. PEVSoft Trainz Mesh Viewer 2. PEVSoft PM2IM.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".DJA",
    "Dundjinni Module File",
    "2.5",
    "A DJA file is a module created by Dundjinni, a program used to create fantasy maps that can be played as adventures. It contains module information, which includes a map and an adventure. DJA files are created when a user selects File → Save or Save as. The file can be opened by selecting File → Open in Dundjinni. The DJA file is the main file type associated with Dundjinni, along with the DJC (contains characters), DJM (contains monsters), and DJX (contains art) files. Dundjinni allows you to create maps by drawing walls and floors on a grid using a variety of tools. You can use the maps to create an adventure by adding NPCs, objects, rooms, monsters, and treasure. NOTE: DJA files are saved by default in the Adventure folder located in the Dundjinni root folder. Windows Dundjinni —  (Discontinued). Trial Mac Dundjinni —  (Discontinued). Trial.",
    "Windows Dundjinni —  (Discontinued). Trial. Mac Dundjinni —  (Discontinued). Trial.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".FPK",
    "Civilization 4 Data File",
    "2.5",
    "Game assets file used by Sid Meiers Civilization IV, a turn-based strategy game; saves art data for game graphics; stored in the Civilization IV/​Assets/​ installation directory; can be extracted using PakBuild for Windows or Macapaka for Mac. Example Civilization IV art asset files include Art0.fpk, Assets0.fpk, Assets1.fpk, Assets2.fpk, and Assets3.fpk. NOTE: FPK files are also used by Sid Meiers Pirates. Windows Take-Two Interactive Civilization 4. Take-Two Interactive Sid Meiers Pirates. PakBuild. Mac MacapakaFree. Forms file created by software products developed by JetForm or Accelio; discontinued after the software products were acquired by Adobe Systems, who now uses the.PDF format for form documents. Windows Adobe LiveCycle ES4.",
    "Windows Take-Two Interactive Civilization 4. Take-Two Interactive Sid Meiers Pirates. PakBuild. Mac Macapaka. Windows Adobe LiveCycle ES4.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".NCER",
    "Nitro Cell Resource File",
    "2.5",
    "An NCER file is a graphic resource data file used by various games for the Nintendo DS handheld console. It contains information about the arrangement of graphic tiles that make up images used in the game. NCER files are part of the Nitro file system, which is a collection of resource files used by Nintendo DS games to define images, textures, audio, and text. The files are not meant to be viewed or edited by a user, instead, they are referenced by the Nintendo DS game. However, Nintendo DS game ROMs may be dumped to computers by nostalgic gamers in order to play the games on their computers. Users can then rip NCER files and other Nitro resource files from the ROMs to view and modify the files. NOTE: The Nintendo DS device was a handheld gaming console released in 2004. Windows TinkeFree.",
    "Windows Tinke.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".E2GM",
    "Pangea Enigmo 2 Custom Game File",
    "2.5",
    "Custom game file used by Enigmo 2, an outer space puzzle game; contains one or more game levels, including walls, locations of obstacles, dynamic puzzle parts, player parts, and solution conditions; used for storing custom puzzles as well as downloading new puzzles from the Internet. When saving from a custom game, the resulting file stores all of the custom game data, allowing the custom puzzle to be played even if the E2GM file is deleted. Custom games can be created by selecting Edit Custom Game → Create New from the Enigmo 2 main menu. Mac Pangea Enigmo 2.",
    "Mac Pangea Enigmo 2.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BB3",
    "BlasterBall 3 Level File Support",
    "2.5",
    "File created by BlasterBall 3, an arcade game in which the user plays by breaking through patterns of bricks; contains level file support data; used for allowing the game to quickly load player progress as well as custom levels created by the user in the Level Editor feature of BlasterBall 3. Windows WildTangent BlasterBall 3 —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows WildTangent BlasterBall 3 —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".IMAGELIST",
    "Wheres My ... ? Image List",
    "2.5",
    "An IMAGELIST file is a plain text file included in the mobile puzzle game Wheres My Water? or another game in the Wheres My.. ? series. It lists the textures included in the game. Wheres My.. ? games use IMAGELIST files to retrieve and show textures in-game. Wheres My Water? is a puzzle video game published by Disney Mobile. It is available for Android and iOS. The game has several sequels, including Wheres My Perry?, Wheres My Mickey?, and Wheres My Water? 2. All Wheres My.. ? games contain IMAGELIST files. These files list the textures included in the game and accompanying metadata, such as the images sizes and offsets. Wheres My.. ? games refer to these image lists and use them to load textures used to display game menus and objects. You can open an IMAGELIST file in Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or any other text editor. You may have to change the files extension to.TXT before you can open it. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor iOS Wheres My Water?. Android Wheres My Water?.",
    "Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. Any text editor. iOS Wheres My Water?. Android Wheres My Water?.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".MD",
    "Sharkport Saved Game File",
    "2.5",
    "An MD file is a text file created using one of several possible dialects of the Markdown language. It is saved in plain text format but includes inline symbols that define how to format the text (e.g. bold, indentations, headers, table formatting). MD files are designed for authoring plain text documentation that can be easily converted to HTML. MD file open in Caret MD files are not only useful for HTML documentation systems, but also for source code version control. This is because the files can be compared against historical revisions in human-readable text (whereas revisions to binary files cannot be compared easily). Projects created with GitHub, a popular online version control system, often use a file named README.md, which contains the readme for the project. John Gruber, the developer of Markdown, has created a Perl program for converting Markdown to HTML. The program, called Markdown, is available on the Daring Fireball website. NOTE: Markdown files also use the.MARKDOWN extension. You can open and edit an MD file in any text editor, including: Microsoft Notepad (Windows) Apple TextEdit (Mac) Vim (Linux, Mac) GitHub Atom (cross-platform) Google Chrome Text (Chrome OS) However, if you intend to edit an MD file, you may want to open it in a Markdown editor. Markdown editors provide editing and review tools that will help you apply Markdown syntax correctly. Some Markdown editors include: ghostwriter (Windows, Linux) MacDown (Mac) Caret (cross-platform) StackEdit (Web). Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Microsoft WordPad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). gVim. ghostwriter. Caret. Typora. Daring Fireball Markdown. Other text editor Mac MacroMates TextMate. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). MacVim. Vim. MacDown. Caret. Typora. Daring Fireball Markdown. Other text editor Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. ghostwriter. Caret. Typora. Daring Fireball Markdown. Other text editor Web HackMD. StackEdit. Android File Viewer for Android. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS. Game ROM used by emulation software for the SEGA Mega Drive, an older game console (called the SEGA Genesis in North America); stores the contents of a game cartridge; used for running older games on the PC. NOTE: SBWin can be used to convert MD files to the.BIN SEGA game ROM format, which can be played by many different SEGA Master Drive/Genesis emulators. Windows SBWinFree. Programming file that contains an instruction pattern for each instruction that the target machine supports; referenced by the GNU Compiler Collection (GCC), commonly used for compiling programs on Unix systems. Windows gVim. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor Mac GNU Compiler Collection (GCC). MacroMates TextMate. Other text editor Linux GNU Compiler Collection (GCC). Vi GNU Emacs. Other text editor. An MD file is a compressed archive created by MDCD, an archiving utility available for MS-DOS. It contains one or more compressed files. MD files are compressed using Lempel-Ziv-Welch (LZW) compression. Developer Mike Davenport created MDCD in 1988. The compressed archives MDCD creates are similar to.ZOO files, in that both are compressed using LZW compression. However, while zoo was available primarily for Unix systems, MDCD was available only for MS-DOS. NOTE: Some MDCD archives may use the.cd extension, instead of.md. You can open an MD file and extract the files it contains with Deark (multiplatform) or MDCD. Because MDCD is available only for MS-DOS, you may have to run it in an MS-DOS emulator, such as DOSbox. Windows Deark. MDCDFree. An MD file is a MuseData musical score. It contains plain text code that represents a piece of music and metadata describing that work. While MD files are no longer widely used, you can still open them with MuseScore and create sheet music from them. MD file open in MuseScore In 1983, developer Walter B. Hewlett created the MuseData music notation file format to represent the logical content of musical scores in a software-neutral fashion. To do this, Hewlett developed a format that utilized plain text notation to represent the measures, notes, rests, and emphases included in a piece of music. MD files also include a plain text header containing general information about the file, including when the file was created, what musical score, movement, or part it represents, and the instruments used to play it. As digital music notation developed further, MD files largely became obsolete. However, many MD files are still available online, and you can open them with MuseScore, a free music composition and notation program. You can open an MD file with MuseScore by selecting File → Open. If you receive an error message notifying you that your MD file is corrupted. If you do, click Ignore. The MD file will then appear in MuseScore as a musical score. If you need only to see the plain text notation that an MD file contains, you can open it with any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad, Apple TextEdit, or Github Atom. Windows MuseScore. Any text editor Mac MuseScore. Any text editor Linux MuseScore. Any text editor. File created by Sharkport, a hardware accessory for the PlayStation 2; contains a PS2 saved game created by the Sharkport device; used for copying saved games to the PC and sharing them with other players; can be converted to other saved game formats, such as.PSU, using the PS2 Save Builder. NOTE: Sharkport also now uses the.PS2 extension for saved games. Windows PS2 Save BuilderFree. Data file saved by Moneydance, a personal finance software program similar to Intuit Quicken or Microsoft Money; stores bank accounts, transactions, budgets, stock portfolios, and other information. Moneydance supports Mac, Windows, Linux, OS/2, Solaris, and Unix platforms. Windows Reilly Technologies Moneydance. Mac Reilly Technologies Moneydance. Linux Reilly Technologies Moneydance.",
    "Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Microsoft WordPad Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). gVim. ghostwriter. Caret. Typora. Daring Fireball Markdown. Other text editor. Mac MacroMates TextMate. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). MacVim. Vim. MacDown. Caret. Typora. Daring Fireball Markdown. Other text editor. Linux Vim. GitHub Atom —  (Discontinued). GNU Emacs. ghostwriter. Caret. Typora. Daring Fireball Markdown. Other text editor. Web HackMD. StackEdit. Android File Viewer for Android. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS. Windows SBWin. Windows gVim. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor. Mac GNU Compiler Collection (GCC). MacroMates TextMate. Other text editor. Linux GNU Compiler Collection (GCC). Vi GNU Emacs. Other text editor. Windows Deark. MDCD. Windows MuseScore. Any text editor. Mac MuseScore. Any text editor. Linux MuseScore. Any text editor. Windows PS2 Save Builder. Windows Reilly Technologies Moneydance. Mac Reilly Technologies Moneydance. Linux Reilly Technologies Moneydance.",
    "MuseScore can convert MD files to several different formats:.MSCZ - MuseScore Compressed Score.MSCX - MuseScore Music Score.MXL - Compressed MusicXML File.MUSICXML - MusicXML File.MID,.MIDI - MIDI File.PDF - Portable Document Format.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics.WAV - WAVE Audio File.MP3 - MP3 Audio File.FLAC -. Lossless Audio Codec File.OGG - Ogg Vorbis Audio File."],
    ["game_files",
    ".SOEPSX",
    "Player Studio Viewer Item File",
    "2.5",
    "A SOEPSX file is an item file created by Player Studio Viewer (PSV), an application distributed with Daybreak Games such as EverQuest, EverQuest II, Landmark, and PlanetSide 2 games. It contains an item such as helmets, decals, or armor, texture maps, and geometry files. SOEPSX files are saved in the Sony Online Entertainment Player Studio (SOEPSX) format. Player Studio allows you to create and edit in-game items. These items can be uploaded to the Daybreak Games marketplace to be sold as long as you have a valid Daybreak account. The items can also be created just to import into the game. You can view and edit your items with the PSV before submitting them. The PSV application can be found in the PlayerStudio subfolder of the game installation directory. Each PSV is unique to the game it is bundled with. PSV is used to prepare submission bundles and save the item in the SOEPSX format. Once you are ready to submit your item to the marketplace you must take a screenshot of your submission in.JPG format and name the screenshot to match the submission. NOTE: Daybreak Game Company is an American game developer that was formerly known as Sony Online Entertainment. Windows Daybreak Games EverQuest. Daybreak Games EverQuest II. Daybreak Games PlanetSide 2.",
    "Windows Daybreak Games EverQuest. Daybreak Games EverQuest II. Daybreak Games PlanetSide 2.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".JG4",
    "BigJig 4 Jigsaw Puzzle",
    "2.5",
    "Jigsaw puzzle file used by BigJig, a computer-based jigsaw puzzle game; contains a photo or painting that is broken into puzzle pieces; may use eight different shape styles including classic, modern, curl, artistic, bony, scrappy, distorted, and spriggy. BigJig puzzles can also be created with JigMake, a puzzle creation program included with BigJig. Windows Lena Games BigJigFree.",
    "Windows Lena Games BigJig.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".JAP",
    "Japanese Nintendo 64 Game ROM",
    "2.5",
    "File used by nonogram puzzle programs, such as QNonograms; contains a nonogram puzzle, which consists of numbers and cells in a grid. Nonogram puzzles, which are also known as griddlers, paint-by-numbers, hanjie, etc., are puzzles made up of cells in a grid that must be colored or left blank in order to reveal a picture. The puzzles contain numbers for each grid row and column that indicate the number of colored square sets. With this information, you must choose which squares are colored and which squares are blank in order to solve the puzzle and reveal the image. Windows QNonograms. Linux QNonogramsFree. Game file used by Nintendo 64 emulators such as Project64; saves a copy of the original game cartridge and can be played on a PC with supporting emulation software. The .jap file extension means that the game is localized in Japanese. However, .jap is rarely used for ROMs. Nintendo 64 ROMs more commonly use the.N64 file extension. Windows Project64. DaedalusFree. A JAP file is a project settings file created by jAlbum, a program used to create and manage photo galleries. It contains settings for a jAlbum album, which include the style, type of skin, skin font, and skin text color of the album. A JAP file is created by jAlbum when you save a project for the first time by selecting Menu → File → Save. The JAP file is generated along with several other project files, which include.PROPERTIES,.TXT, and.HTT files. JAP files are saved by default in the My Albums folder. However, you can change the default location by selecting Menu → jAlbum → Preferences → Album in Windows. In macOS, you can select Menu → Tools → Preferences. jAlbum is similar to a photo manager, such as Microsoft Photos and Apple Photos. The software allows you to organize photos into albums, use basic editing tools, and upload albums to the web as HTML- or Flash-based galleries. jalbum-settings.jap - The default name given to jAlbum JAP projects. Windows jAlbum. Mac jAlbum.",
    "Windows QNonograms. Linux QNonograms. Windows Project64. Daedalus. Windows jAlbum. Mac jAlbum.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".NL2SCRIPT",
    "NoLimits 2 Script File",
    "2.5",
    "Script description file used by NoLimits 2 Roller Coaster Simulation (NL2), a roller coaster simulator; contains a script, which includes relative paths to classes, the preview picture, and other resource files; can be run by the NoLimits Virtual Machine (NLVM) script engine for NL2. NL2SCRIPT files are XML-formatted and used to describe NL2 scripts. They are commonly used to modify game sounds, sound triggers during gameplay, and more. Windows Mad Data NoLimits Rollercoaster Simulation 2.",
    "Windows Mad Data NoLimits Rollercoaster Simulation 2.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".BUSSIDMOD",
    "Bus Simulator Indonesia Mod",
    "2.5",
    "A BUSSIDMOD file contains a mod for Maleo Bus Simulator Indonesia, a bus driving simulation game for Android. It is used to alter the appearance of a players vehicle. Players can download BUSSIDMOD files from the Internet and install them in Bus Simulator Indonesia. Bus Simulator Indonesia, also known as BUSSID, is a mobile game in which players drive a bus across Indonesia. The game enjoys a healthy modding scene, which creates vehicle customization mods saved in BUSSIDMOD files. Modders then share their BUSSIDMOD files online. Other players may download a BUSSIDMOD file from a BUSSID-related forum or a file-sharing website. Sometimes, these BUSSIDMOD files are packaged in.ZIP or otherwise-compressed archives. To retrieve their BUSSIDMOD file, players must first decompress the archive in which it is stored. To use a BUSSIDMOD file with Bus Simulator Indonesia (Android): Open Bus Simulator Indonesia and select MOD from the Management menu. In the MOD window, select Import. When the Import MOD window appears, select File Manager. In the File Manager window, navigate to and select your BUSSIDMOD file. Click through the Install Mod Fee window. The mod your BUSSIDMOD file contains will then appear in the MOD windows vehicle selection list. Android Maleo Bus Simulator IndonesiaFree.",
    "Android Maleo Bus Simulator Indonesia.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".ES3",
    "Kiwi Clicker Saved Game",
    "2.5",
    "An ES3 file is a saved game created by tobspr Games Kiwi Clicker. It contains data a player can use to resume an in-progress game. Kiwi Clicker is a video game in which players click their mouse to manage a kiwi bird production facility. During the game, players can choose to save their progress. Doing so creates a new ES3 file, which the player can use to resume their saved game at a later time. The game stores ES3 files in the following directory: ~/​Users/​YourUserName/​AppData/​LocalLow/​Tobspr Games/​Kiwi Clicker. You can resume the saved game an ES3 file contains in Kiwi Clicker (Windows). To do so, place the file in the following directory: ~/​Users/​YourUserName/​AppData/​LocalLow/​Tobspr Games/​Kiwi Clicker Then, open Kiwi Clicker and resume the saved game your ES3 file contains. Windows tobspr Games Kiwi Clicker.",
    "Windows tobspr Games Kiwi Clicker.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".CPG",
    "StarCraft Campaign File",
    "2.5",
    "Character encoding file used by ESRI software products such as the ArcGIS Desktop suite; describes a set of characters for displaying text in shapefiles; helps localize maps for specific languages. Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro. Page file created by Manga Studio, a program used to create digital comic art; contains page layout settings as well as cartoon sketches, textures, captions, word balloons, and special effects; can be exported to.BMP,.JPG,.PSD,.PNG,.TIFF,.TGA, and.PICT formats. Manga Studio became Clip Studio Paint in 2015. It is also known as ComicStudio in Japan. Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Campaign file for StarCraft, a real-time strategy game that takes place in space; includes mission data and artificial intelligence information, which determines the difficulty of the mission. NOTE: StarCraft maps are saved as.SCM files. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. Web page project created by Cool Page, an older drag and drop Web page editor; may contain various Web page objects and their properties; allows users to save designed pages. Since CPG files are saved in a proprietary format, they can only be opened in Cool Page. However, these files can be published to standard HTML. NOTE: The last version of Cool Page was released in 2002, and the last supported operating system was Windows XP. Windows 3Dize Cool Page. A CPG file is a codeplug file used by a Motorola Solutions two-way radio. It contains channel settings and other data used to program a radio. CPG files are radio-specific, and they are edited using Motorola Solutions customer programming software (CPS). Motorola Solutions two-way radio users who want to adjust the frequencies their radio operates upon can do so by loading and editing the radios CPG file in a CPS program. For example, a user with access to the MOTOTRBO CPS can connect their radio to their computer and use MOTOTRBO to READ and edit their radios CPG file. A radios CPG file also contains other information specific to that radio. For example, the CPG file lists the radios serial number and FLASHcode features. Because a radios CPG file contains so much essential data, and editing the file incorrectly can cause your radio to malfunction, it is recommended that you save a backup of your radios original CPG file before editing it. That way, you can re-install your radios original CPG file if needed. The following Motorola Solutions two-way radios are known to use CPG format codeplugs. HT750 HT1250 MTX9250. You can open and edit a CPG file in Motorola Solutions MOTOTRBO CPS (Windows), which must be purchased from Motorola. After purchasing and installing MOTOTRBO, open the program, select Open from its toolbar, and then navigate to and open your CPG file. Windows Motorola Solutions MOTOTRBO CPS.",
    "Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro. Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Windows Blizzard StarCraft. Mac Blizzard StarCraft. Windows 3Dize Cool Page. Windows Motorola Solutions MOTOTRBO CPS.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".STL",
    "SuperTux Level File",
    "2.4",
    "An STL file is a 3D model saved in the stereolithography file format developed by 3D Systems. It contains plain text or binary data that describes a set of triangular facets, which comprise a model. STL files are quite common, and they can be opened in many CAD and 3D modeling programs. STL file open in Microsoft 3D Viewer Stereolithography is a form of 3D printing primarily used for creating product prototypes. In the late 1980s, 3D Systems co-founder Chuck Hull patented stereolithography technology, and 3D Systems created the STL file format. Primarily, STL files contain 3D models meant to be printed using stereolithography. Because the STL format was one of the first formats used to store models for 3D printing, a large number of 3D model viewers and CAD programs support it. STL files may be saved as plain text files, which contain human-readable triangular tessellation data, or as binary files, which contain the same data saved in a binary format. When opened in a text editor, plain text STL files appear as a list of facets and vertexes, complete with coordinates. These files always begin with the string solid ModelName. NOTE: STL files are also sometimes referred to as Standard Triangle Language files and Standard Tessellation Language files. Plain text STL file open in Apple TextEdit You can open an STL file in many image viewers, 3D modeling, and CAD programs, including: Microsoft 3D Viewer (Windows) Apple Preview (Mac) MeshLab (multiplatform) Autodesk Fusion 360 (multiplatform) You can also open plain text STL files in text editors, such as Microsoft Notepad and Apple TextEdit, to view the plain text data they contain. (If you open a binary STL file in a text editor, its data will appear as a series of unintelligible characters.). All Platforms PTC Onshape. Android Shyam Barange 3D Model Viewer. Prisma3D. Autodesk Fusion 360. Windows Microsoft 3D Viewer. Microsoft 3D Builder. Microsoft Print 3D. Autodesk Fusion 360. IMSI TurboCAD Pro. GOM Inspect. ideaMK STL Viewer. Parametric Technology Creo. Dassault Systemes CATIA. MeshLab. CADSoftTools ABViewer. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Kubotek KeyCreator. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Autodesk Fusion 360. IMSI TurboCAD Deluxe. Cheetah3D. MeshLab. GLC_Player. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Linux Autodesk Fusion 360. Parametric Technology Creo. Dassault Systemes CATIA. MeshLab. GLC_Player. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Web Online 3D Viewer. Autodesk Tinkercad. Autodesk Fusion 360. 3D Slash. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. List of predefined items that have been signed by a trusted entity; may consist of a list of filenames or a list of certificates; each item in the list has been approved by the signing entity. Certificate trust lists (CTLs) are used by Microsoft IIS to store trusted websites and other addresses that require a secure connection. Windows Microsoft Internet Information Services (IIS). Library of styles referenced by Macromedia (now Adobe) Fireworks; may be used to apply Stroke, Fill, Effect, and Text attributes to an object within an open Fireworks project; can be helpful for creating a uniform look across multiple objects. Some styles are included with Fireworks, though additional styles may be added to the program. To add extra styles, click the small icon in the top right corner of the Styles panel in Fireworks and select Import Styles. Then browse to an STL file and click OK to add the style library to your current collection. Windows Adobe Fireworks —  (Discontinued). Trial Mac Adobe Fireworks —  (Discontinued). Trial. Game file used by SuperTux, a 2D jump and run side scrolling game similar to Super Mario Bros.; saved in a plain text format and specifies the features of a level, such as enemy unit locations, positions of blocks, and the time limit; also includes a reference to the music and background image for the level. STL files are stored in the /​data/​levels/​ directory of the installation. Windows SuperTux. Mac SuperTux. Linux SuperTuxFree. An STL file is a subtitles file saved in the European Broadcasting Union (EBU) subtitle data exchange format. It contains binary data used to load subtitles and store subtitle metadata. STL files are used mostly to provide subtitles during TV broadcasts. In 1991, the EBU published specifications for the STL subtitles format. STL files contain a set of subtitle texts and information, such as time codes and positioning, used to display that text during a broadcast. The files also contain metadata that defines the subtitles publisher, editor, and country of origin. Unlike many other types of subtitle files, STL files are binary files, so you cannot view or edit the text they contain in a text editor. Some broadcasters still use the STL format, but the format has largely been replaced by the newer, XML-based EBU-TT format. You can open an STL file with EZTitles (Windows) or Avid Media Composer (Windows, Mac). These programs allow you to import STL files and use them as subtitle tracks while creating a video. You can also view the subtitles and metadata an STL file contains with Jongbel Media Solutions EBU STL Viewer (Windows). Windows EZTitles. Avid Media Composer. Jongbel Media Solutions EBU STL Viewer. Mac Avid Media Composer.",
    "All Platforms PTC Onshape. Android Shyam Barange 3D Model Viewer. Prisma3D. Autodesk Fusion 360. Windows Microsoft 3D Viewer. Microsoft 3D Builder. Microsoft Print 3D. Autodesk Fusion 360. IMSI TurboCAD Pro. GOM Inspect. ideaMK STL Viewer. Parametric Technology Creo. Dassault Systemes CATIA. MeshLab. CADSoftTools ABViewer. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Kubotek KeyCreator. Mac Apple Preview Included with OS. Autodesk Fusion 360. IMSI TurboCAD Deluxe. Cheetah3D. MeshLab. GLC_Player. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Linux Autodesk Fusion 360. Parametric Technology Creo. Dassault Systemes CATIA. MeshLab. GLC_Player. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Web Online 3D Viewer. Autodesk Tinkercad. Autodesk Fusion 360. 3D Slash. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. Windows Microsoft Internet Information Services (IIS). Windows Adobe Fireworks —  (Discontinued). Trial. Mac Adobe Fireworks —  (Discontinued). Trial. Windows SuperTux. Mac SuperTux. Linux SuperTux. Windows EZTitles. Avid Media Composer. Jongbel Media Solutions EBU STL Viewer. Mac Avid Media Composer.",
    "Several CAD and 3D model editing programs, including Autodesk Fusion 360 and Microsoft 3D Builder, can convert STL files to other 3D model formats. For example, Fusion 360 can export STL files to:.F3D - Fusion 360 Archive.3MF - 3D Manufacturing File.IPT - Inventor Part.FBX - Autodesk FBX Interchange File.OBJ - Wavefront 3D Object.SKP - SketchUp Document.SMT - Autodesk Shape Manager Text File.STP - STEP 3D Model.USDZ - Universal Scene Description Zipped Apple Preview and Microsoft 3D Viewer can convert STL files to raster images. For example, Microsoft 3D Viewer can convert an STL file to the following formats:.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.JPEG -JPEG Image.BMP - Bitmap Image.TIFF - Tagged Image File Format Apple Preview can also convert STL files to.PDF documents. You can use Jongbel Media Solutions EBU STL Viewer (Windows) or EZConvert (Windows) to convert STL files to many other subtitle formats, including:.SRT - SubRip Subtitles.ASS - Aegisub Advanced SubStation Alpha.PAC - PAC Subtitles.VTT - Web Video Text Tracks.SUB - MicroDVD Subtitles.890 - Cavena Subtitles.USF - Universal Subtitles Format."],
    ["game_files",
    ".MAP",
    "Leges Motus Map File",
    "2.4",
    "A MAP file is a game map created for games developed using the Quake engine or a related game development engine, such as the Valve Goldsource Engine. It is saved in a human-readable plain text format. MAP files are uncompiled but can be compiled into binary.BSP files for use in games such as Half-Life, Quake, Quake 2, and Quake 3. Developers and modders can create MAP files using several map editors, including Valve Hammer Editor. These programs can typically compile MAP files into the correct target BSP format, for use in a specific game or games. TorquePowered.coms Torque Constructor is another popular tool that uses MAP files. It can convert maps into the.DIF (Torque Game Engine Model) format for further development. The resulting maps can be included in Torque games, which are available for PC, mobile, and console platforms. What game engines create MAP files? Many game engines create game maps saved in the MAP format. Some examples include: Quake Engine Goldsource Engine Unreal Engine Torque Engine Dark Engine NOTE: Valve Hammer Editor 4, which is used to develop and create mods for Half-life, saves maps in the newer.VMF format. The program was previously called Worldcraft but is now commonly referred to as Hammer. You can open a MAP file with Valve Hammer Editor (Windows), Chain Studios J.A.C.K. (multiplatform), Quark (Windows), and many other Quake engine-related development and modding programs. You can also open a MAP file with any text editor to view the plain text data it contains. Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Chain Studios J.A.C.K. Torque Constructor —  (Discontinued). id Software GtkRadiant. QuArK. MAP3BSPC. Q3Map2. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor Linux Chain Studios J.A.C.K.Free. Game map used by Halo: Combat Evolved, the first game of the Halo first-person shooter series; also used by Halo: Custom Edition, an unsupported expansion to Halo: Combat Evolved; saves a game map and can include terrain, objects, spawn points, and other level information. Some Halo maps can be edited with Halo Map Tools. Windows Bungie Halo: Combat Evolved Halo Map Tools. Mac Bungie Halo: Combat Evolved. File used by Fallout 1 and 2, which are post-apocalyptic, futuristic role-playing video games; contains map data that describes the gameplay environment including grid boundaries, walls, scenery, animals, and objects. The MAP file is made up of 5 sections: The MAP file header. The global and local variables used by the map scripts. The tile data that makes up the roof and floor. The MAP scripts that store information about scripts connected to the objects in the map. The MAP objects, which hold the walls, item, scenery, etc. that appear in the map. Windows Bethesda Softworks Fallout. Bethesda Softworks Fallout 2. A MAP file is a game data file used by Re-Logic Terraria, a 2D action-adventure and sandbox construction game. It contains a map of the area explored by a character for a certain world, which may include terrain, water, monsters, items, and other objects. You will most likely only encounter a Terraria MAP file if you have Terraria installed on your computer and are navigating the data files for characters in the Steam/​userdata directory. The MAP files are not meant to be manually opened by a user. Instead, they are referenced by Terraria to load information for a specific character that details the area the character has explored in a certain world. Windows Re-Logic Terraria. Game map, referred to as a Dream, used by Furcadia, a 2D multiplayer online game set in a fantasy world; saves the map width, height, effects such as rain, and objects such as trees, walls, buildings, and magical plants. MAP files can be edited using the Furcadia Dream Editor (DreamEd.exe), which is included with the Furcadia installation. Custom maps can be used for playing with others online. Windows Furcadia. A MAP file is a server-side text file used to link sections of a webpage image to different locations. Applying a MAP file to an image allows users to click on different areas of the image to open different webpages. While webpages reference MAP files, the files are stored and processed on web servers. You can open and edit a MAP file with Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or any other text editor. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor Linux Vim. Any text editor. Game map used by Leges Motus, a 2D multiplayer shooting game set zero gravity; stores the layout for the map, including spawn points, walls, and the locations of map objects and corresponding sprites; located in the /​data/​maps/​ directory of the game installation. Windows Leges Motus. Mac Leges Motus. Linux Leges MotusFree. Map file used by NAVIGON GPS navigation devices; contains a map, including roads and points of interest; used by NAVIGON software to create navigation routes and display map information while driving. Windows NAVIGON Sync. Weather map format used by Weather Defender, a weather monitoring system designed specifically for Emergency Management Professionals and First Responders; may contain custom geographic and reference layers. Weather Defender maps can be saved to store custom configurations for forecasting severe weather. These maps can be quickly loaded to view custom weather forecasts. Windows SWIFT Weather Defender. Text mapping file used by TECkit, a program used for text conversion; saved in a plain text format and contains rules that map from one character set to another; compiled into a.TEC file, which can be used to perform the conversion. Windows TECkit. pyTecKit. Mac TECkit. pyTecKit. Linux TECkit. pyTecKitFree. Key assignment file used by Rigs of Rods (RoR), a car, truck, airplane, and boat simulator; contains information that describes how the users keyboard is mapped out and which keys correlate with specific actions in RoR. The information is stored in plain text and appears in the following format: EVENT_NAME EVENT_TYPE MAPPING. input.map - The common name for the MAP file containing the key assignments for the simulator. Windows Rigs of Rods. Mac Rigs of RodsFree. File used by Mapjects GRYD, an operations visualization platform for energy management, security management, and logistics; stores a configuration of one or more Webparts, which are widgets that can be mashed together to produce integrated visualizations; also includes the GIS metadata required to display the data. MAP files are server-side data files, and they include both the data and program files for the software package. A corresponding.MAPX file is used to display the information in the MAP file to the user through a Web page. NOTE: Mapject GRYD renders HTML5, Silverlight, Flash, and PHP, as well as code from the ASP.NET Razor view engine. Windows Mapjects GRYD Linux Mapjects GRYD. A MAP file is a game map used by Super Mario War, an open source Super Mario-like video game. It contains the layout of a level in the game, which includes the location of blocks, items, and sprites. MAP files are located in the Maps folder of the game installation directory. MAP files are loaded by the game when a user selects the level. You can also create and modify MAP levels using the level editor tool (Leveleditor.exe) included with the Super Mario War download. Super Mario War features many of the same elements as other Super Mario series games. The main element of gameplay is players jumping on the heads of other players to defeat them. Players can also use items placed throughout each level to defeat other players. Windows Super Mario War. Mac Super Mario War. Linux Super Mario WarFree.",
    "Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Chain Studios J.A.C.K. Torque Constructor —  (Discontinued). id Software GtkRadiant. QuArK. MAP3BSPC. Q3Map2. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Linux Chain Studios J.A.C.K. Windows Bungie Halo: Combat Evolved Halo Map Tools. Mac Bungie Halo: Combat Evolved. Windows Bethesda Softworks Fallout. Bethesda Softworks Fallout 2. Windows Re-Logic Terraria. Windows Furcadia. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor. Linux Vim. Any text editor. Windows Leges Motus. Mac Leges Motus. Linux Leges Motus. Windows NAVIGON Sync. Windows SWIFT Weather Defender. Windows TECkit. pyTecKit. Mac TECkit. pyTecKit. Linux TECkit. pyTecKit. Windows Rigs of Rods. Mac Rigs of Rods. Windows Mapjects GRYD. Linux Mapjects GRYD. Windows Super Mario War. Mac Super Mario War. Linux Super Mario War.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".PQ",
    "Progress Quest Save File",
    "2.4",
    "Save file used by Progress Quest, a computer role-playing game; contains character information, such as the characters race, class, and stats, and game progress. Progress Quest is a variation of other computer role-playing games such as EverQuest. After you set up your character, you dont participate in the game at all. The game plays itself while you watch. When you play the game, your progress is automatically saved when you close out the application or when you level up. When you close the application, a dialog appears with the directory that the PQ file is located in. It is saved in the same directory in which the Progress Quest application is saved. The file is named after the name of your character. To load a PQ saved game, select Load Game from the game start screen, navigate to your file, and select Open. NOTE: A.BAK backup file is created whenever the PQ file is saved. If the PQ file becomes corrupt, you can load the backup file. Windows Progress Quest. Linux Progress QuestFree. File used by Picturesque, an image editor; contains effects settings that alter the appearance of the image; includes shadow opacity, blur radius, reflection length, corner curvature, stroke width, color, and perspective. To create a PQ file, select the Presets icon in the lower-right corner, click the + symbol, name the preset, and make your changes. Mac Acqualia Picturesque.",
    "Windows Progress Quest. Linux Progress Quest. Mac Acqualia Picturesque.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".TIL",
    "CTGP Revolution Texture Archive",
    "2.4",
    "A TIL file is an archive that contains textures used by CTGP Revolution (CTGP-R), a fan-made mod to Mario Kart Wii that adds extra features, like new tracks and game modes. It stores a collection of graphics referenced in CTGP-R, which includes buttons, menu option titles, and icons. You will only encounter TIL files if you download the CTGP-R mod and dig around the resource files packaged with it. The file is not meant to be manually opened by users. Instead, it is referenced by the Wii or Wii U console to load resources for menus and in-game graphics. However, some users looking to modify the appearance of the CTGP-R menu will manually open a TIL file to alter the textures stored within it. After making their changes, they will package the textures back into the TIL archive in the CTGP-R mod, transfer it to an SD card, and insert the SD card in the Wii or Wii U to play the mod. The user must have a valid copy of Mario Kart Wii to play the mod. textures.tile - Name of the TIL file packaged with CTGP-R. It can be found in the ctgpr folder after extracting it from the CTGP-R.zip file downloaded from the CTGP-R website. Windows CTGP Revolution. BrawlBoxFree.",
    "Windows CTGP Revolution. BrawlBox.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".NUMDLB",
    "Namco Universal Model Binary",
    "2.4",
    "A NUMDLB file is a 3D model used by a Bandai Namco video game, such as Super Smash Bros. Ultimate. It contains binary data used to show a character or object in-game. NUMDLB files are most commonly used to mod Super Smash Bros. Ultimate characters appearances. Most Super Smash Bros. Ultimate players will never encounter a NUMDLB file. However, some modders extract and edit NUMDLB files to alter characters in-game appearances. While other Bandai Namco video games use NUMDLB files to store 3D models, those games players do not typically extract and edit NUMDLB files. So, if you have encountered an NUMDLB file, it likely originated from Super Smash Bros. Ultimate. Super Smash Bros. Ultimate modders can open NUMDLB files in Blender (cross-platform) with the io_scene_numdlb add-on installed. Modders can also open NUMDLB files and convert them to and from other 3D model formats, such as.DAE and.FBX, with StudioSB (Windows). Windows Blender. io_scene_numdlb. StudioSB. Mac Blender. io_scene_numdlb. Linux Blender. io_scene_numdlbFree.",
    "Windows Blender. io_scene_numdlb. StudioSB. Mac Blender. io_scene_numdlb. Linux Blender. io_scene_numdlb.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".SST",
    "Children of the Nile Texture",
    "2.4",
    "Digital certificate downloaded from a Certificate Authority (CA); installed as a root certificate on Windows computers and is used to validate the identities of websites and software programs; typically saved in a folder along with other.PFX certificate files. The SST file format preserves all certificate store properties and is useful for transferring certificates between computers. Windows Microsoft Certificate Manager Included with OS. An SST file is a texture used by Children of the Nile (CotN), a video game in which players maintain an ancient Egyptian city. It is used to skin an associated.CEM file. SST files are not meant to be opened outside CotN. Children of the Nile, also known as Immortal Cities: Children of the Nile, is a city simulation game in which players build buildings, issue edicts, and tend to citizens needs. Tilted Mill Entertainment released the first edition of CotN in 2004 and an Enhanced Edition in 2008. The games SST files are used to add textures to 3D models that represent people, animals, and buildings. For example, an SST file might contain a brick texture used to skin an obelisk. NOTE: The game Empire Earth also uses SST files. Empire Earths SST files are formatted slightly differently than CotNs SST files. Children of the Nile SST files cannot be opened outside the game. Empire Earth SST files can be opened and viewed using SST-tool, a fan-made SST library. You can use SST-tool to convert Empire Earth SST files to the.TGA format. You can also use SST-tool to convert TGA images to the Empire Earth SST format. Windows Tilted Mill Entertainment Children of the Nile. Stainless Steel Studios Empire Earth. SST-tool. Mac SST-tool. Linux SST-toolFree. An SST file is a project created in Artec Studio, a 3D scanning, modeling, and data processing application. It contains all of the projects 3D data, including data obtained via scanning and post-processing actions. Versions 16 and above of Artec Studio use SST files; previous versions stored project data in a corresponding folder and A3D project file. Artec Studio is a computer-assisted design (CAD) application that allows users to scan a mechanical component, import that scan as a 3D model, and then modify that model using numerous design tools. Artec Studio also allows users to import and export models in other file formats, such as.STEP, for use with other CAD and computer-assisted manufacturing (CAM) programs. In versions 16 and above, Artec Studio projects are saved as SST files. Each SST file contains all that projects scans, meshes, and CAD objects. How do I create a new SST file in Artec Studio? To create a new SST file in Artec Studio versions 16 and above, select File → New project from the programs menu bar. Then, save your new project. Artec Studio will save the project as an SST file. You can open an SST file in Artec Studio versions 16 and above (Windows). To do so, select File → Open project from the programs menu bar. How do I export the scans, meshes, and CAD objects an SST file contains? After you open an SST file in Artec Studio, you can export the scans, meshes, and CAD objects your SST file contains in various file formats, by selecting File → Export → Scans, File → Export → Meshes, or File → Export → CAD objects. Windows Artec 3D Artec Studio.",
    "Windows Microsoft Certificate Manager Included with OS. Windows Tilted Mill Entertainment Children of the Nile. Stainless Steel Studios Empire Earth. SST-tool. Mac SST-tool. Linux SST-tool. Windows Artec 3D Artec Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["game_files",
    ".GBLORB",
    "Glulx Blorb Game File",
    "2.4",
    "Game file used by Interactive Fiction (IF) interpreters, such as Spatterlight or Zoom; contains a Glulx story in Blorb format, which is a format used to bundle different game resource files into a single archive; different resource files include music, graphics, and level information. GBLORB files are similar to.BLORB files but are used for only Glulx games. A GBLORB file is an.ULX file contained in a Blorb wrapper, which gives it more capabilities, like storing resource files.ZBLORB files, which are similar to GBLORB files as well, are used by Z-machines. Windows Windows Frotz. Mac Zoom. Spatterlight. Linux Zoom. Android TwistyFree.",
    "Windows Windows Frotz. Mac Zoom. Spatterlight. Linux Zoom. Android Twisty.",
    "?"],
